मण्डलम् सङ्केतन ॥ ॰ encode — the port of crates/sadhana/src/encode.rs

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ ADR-0030 REMEDIATION, TASK `D-002h`. THIS FILE IS TAKEN IN PARTS, AND WITH
॰ THIS ONE **THE FILE IS FINISHED**. THE PART THIS CYCLE TOOK IS **THE LAST
॰ THREE, TOGETHER WITH THE FAMILY THEY SHARE WITH `ir.t1`**: placing a value
॰ into a field, assembling a word, what is NOT ported yet — and `सम्भाव्य अ६४`,
॰ the OPTIONAL THAT WRAPS A SIXTY-FOUR, wherever the corpus spelled it.
॰ **8 sites the census sees, of which 3 move, and 3 the census cannot see, of
॰ which ALL THREE MOVE.** `encode.t1` carried 18 `अ६४` and 168 `न६४`; it
॰ carries 15 and 171 now, and every one of the 15 has been read and is
॰ CORRECT. Corpus ledger 553/0/825 -> **550/0/828**, sum still 1378.
॰
॰ THE READING IS THAT A WRAPPER IS NOT A TYPE POSITION TO THE CENSUS AND IS
॰ ONE TO THE COMPILER. The ledger counts the token after `ॱॱ` and after
॰ `ददाति`; `सम्भाव्य` occupies that position and the `अ६४` hides one token
॰ behind it. Three sites in the corpus were spelled that way and all three
॰ answer with an unsigned quantity: `स्थानभागः` returns a ONE-BASED LENGTH
॰ (`split_address_part`, `encode.rs:411`, is two `strip_suffix` calls and
॰ names no integer at all — the length is `str::len`'s `usize`), `मूल्याङ्कः`
॰ is `value_of(..) -> Option<u64>` at `:439`, and `ir.t1`'s `पठितम्` takes
॰ `numeral::value(..) -> Result<u64, NumeralError>` through
॰ `sanskrit_text.t1`'s `सङ्ख्या`, WHICH ALREADY ANSWERS `सम्भाव्य न६४`.
॰ That last one is a CROSS-MODULE DISAGREEMENT that survived `ir.t1`'s own
॰ file-bounded cycle: the producer moved and the consumer did not, because
॰ nothing in a per-file walk looks behind a wrapper. **The family is the
॰ bound BECAUSE the divider could not be** — the same argument the slot-kind
॰ unit made, applied to a shape the census is blind to instead of one it can
॰ see.
॰
॰ AND THE THREE VISIBLE MOVERS ARE TWO READINGS, BOTH ALREADY MADE HERE.
॰ `विस्तृतिः` is `let span = 1u64 << width` (`encode.rs:126`) and cycle 532
॰ named it the one mover of its divider without spending the cycle to take
॰ it; the reading is confirmed and not re-derived. `उच्चदैर्घ्य` and
॰ `नीचदैर्घ्य` are BINDINGS OF `स्थानप्रत्ययदैर्घ्यम्`, which cycle 532
॰ moved to `न६४` — so these two are the producer-moved-consumer-did-not
॰ shape a THIRD time, inside this very file, and they sit in the same
॰ routine as the wrapper above them. Producer, wrapper and both consumers
॰ move in ONE cycle, which is the arrangement that leaves nothing owing.
॰
॰ WHAT IS LEFT IN THIS FILE IS 15 `अ६४` AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS A DEFECT.
॰ `चिह्नितम्` in अन्तर्भावः, in चिह्नितान्तर्भावः and in पदरचना is `fits`'s
॰ `let signed = value as i64` and its slice twin — ADR-0031's second
॰ parameter; both `सीमा` are `let limit = 1i64 << (width - 1)`, negated on
॰ the next line; the seven of `the value that half carries` and the three of
॰ `विन्यासविचलनम्` were adjudicated by cycles 533 and 534; and `मूल्यानि` in
॰ अपाकर्तव्यम् and सङ्कोचनिषेधः is `reduce`'s `&[(&str, i64)]` (`:858`).
॰ **A LATER CYCLE READING THIS FILE AS UNFINISHED FROM ITS COUNT WOULD
॰ RESPELL CORRECT SITES.** The count is not the state; this paragraph is.
॰
॰ WHAT THIS UNIT DID NOT TAKE — AND IT IS NO LONGER A LIST OF DIVIDERS IN
॰ THIS FILE, BECAUSE THERE ARE NONE. What ADR-0030 still owes is ONE FILE:
॰ `vakyavibhaga.t1`, 487 `अ६४` and 0 `न६४`, untouched. Every other source in
॰ `crates/sadhana-t1/src/` is remediated; the 63 `अ६४` outside
॰ `vakyavibhaga.t1` (encode 15, samyojana 32, utsarjana 5, ir 4, nidana 3,
॰ vishlesana 3, vastu 1) are the corpus's genuinely signed sites.
॰
॰ `an_optional_that_wraps_a_sixty_four_is_unsigned_in_all_three_places_it_is_written`
॰ pins the three wrapped sites with their twins, the two visible bindings
॰ against the `न६४` producer they read, `विस्तृतिः` against `1u64 << width`,
॰ the four `चिह्नितम्`/`सीमा` sites this unit read and LEFT, and the
॰ corpus-wide absence of `सम्भाव्य अ६४`.
॰
॰ *The account of THE HEAD DECLARATIONS follows and is kept, because the
॰ per-divider table it corrected is the table this unit emptied:*
॰
॰ THE PART BEFORE THIS ONE WAS **THE HEAD DECLARATIONS** — everything above
॰ `══ slot kind predicates ══`, and THE LAST UNIT OF ANY SIZE IN THIS FILE
॰ WITH SITES THAT MOVE. 6 `अ६४`, the census sees all six, and all six move.
॰ `encode.t1` carried 24 `अ६४` and 162 `न६४`; it carries 18 and 168 now.
॰ Corpus ledger 559/0/819 -> **553/0/825**, sum still 1378.
॰
॰ THE READING IS THAT THESE SIX ARE THREE DIFFERENT KINDS OF THING AND EVERY
॰ ONE OF THEM WAS DECIDED SOMEWHERE ELSE IN THIS REPAIR ALREADY: a loop
॰ bound (शिथिलनावृत्तिसीमा, whose twin is `MAX_RELAXATION_ROUNDS: usize = 8`
॰ at `encode.rs:722` and is only ever the top of a range), a discriminant
॰ family (पाठकोष्ठकम्/दत्तकोष्ठकम्/शोधनकोष्ठकम्, whose twin — `RelSection`
॰ at `kosha.rs:185` — holds NO number at all, no repr and no explicit
॰ discriminant, its one payload variant `Debug(&'static str)` flattened here
॰ into a constant beside प्रतीक्षा ॱ कोष्ठकनाम), and two record FIELDS:
॰ प्रतीक्षा ॱ कोष्ठकम्, which holds that section, and सङ्केतनदोष ॱ पङ्क्ति,
॰ which is `EncodeError::line: usize`, 1-based with no ०. NOTHING NEW IS
॰ ARGUED. What is new is that the three readings MEET IN ONE BLOCK, which is
॰ why the unit is the block and not a family: this block is the file's
॰ RECORD TYPES, so every section that reads a field disagreed with the field
॰ until this cycle.
॰
॰ AND THIS FILE WAS THE ONLY ONE LEFT DISAGREEING ON EITHER SPELLING. A line
॰ is already `न६४` twice in `lex.t1` (`Token::line`, `LexError::line`) and in
॰ `parse.t1`; a section discriminant is already `न६४` in `samyojana.t1`.
॰ WHICH TURNS UP SOMETHING WORTH WRITING DOWN AND NOT FIXING HERE:
॰ `samyojana.t1` declares PUBLIC पाठकोष्ठकम् and दत्तकोष्ठकम् of its own, for
॰ `SymSection` — a DIFFERENT enum. They agree on the two values they share
॰ and the third differs by name (शोधनकोष्ठकम् = Debug = ३ here,
॰ बीजकोष्ठकम् = Bss = ३ there), so nothing is wrong today; but two modules
॰ export one name for two enums and T1 has no module system to keep them
॰ apart (`D-002l`).
॰
॰ THE SECOND RESULT IS A CORRECTION TO THIS HEADER'S OWN TABLE, WHICH NAMED
॰ THESE SIX WRONG FOR FOUR CYCLES — AND THE TABLE IS WHAT A CYCLE PICKS ITS
॰ UNIT FROM. The older table called one of them *one register field*; the
॰ newest replaced that with *two under `which instruction set the image is
॰ for`*. NEITHER IS A SITE: the four register fields are `अ३२` masks, and
॰ लक्ष्य's two members are `गणना` constants carrying no type annotation at
॰ all, so nothing counts them. The six are the ones named above.
॰
॰ WHAT THIS UNIT DID NOT TAKE. The 18 `अ६४` left are: placing a value into a
॰ field (5, of which ONE moves — विस्तृतिः), the value that half carries (7,
॰ ALL SEVEN CORRECT), laying out and emitting (3, ALL THREE CORRECT),
॰ assembling a word (1) and what is NOT ported yet (2). **THE HEAD
॰ DECLARATIONS ARE AT 0 AND DROP OFF THIS LIST, AND THE LAST UNIT OF ANY
॰ SIZE GOES WITH THEM: what is left that MOVES is विस्तृतिः's 1 and
॰ assembling a word's 1, against ten sites that are CORRECT and two
॰ unported.**
॰
॰ `the_head_declarations_are_unsigned_because_a_limit_a_section_and_a_line_are`
॰ pins the six sites with their values, the four twin fragments, `RelSection`
॰ having no number, the payload flattening, the five `न६४` mirrors in three
॰ remediated files, the four `अ३२` register fields and the लक्ष्य गणना that
॰ the table miscounted, and the block at (0, 14).
॰
॰ *The account of THE VALUE THAT HALF CARRIES follows and is kept, because
॰ its reading — a divider finished at its full count with nothing moved — is
॰ the one this unit is the counterpart of:*
॰
॰ THE PART BEFORE THIS ONE WAS **THE VALUE THAT HALF CARRIES**, the divider
॰ entire, and it is the FIRST DIVIDER OF THE WHOLE REPAIR IN WHICH NOT ONE
॰ SITE MOVES. 7 `अ६४`, the census sees all seven, and all seven are CORRECT.
॰ `encode.t1` carried 24 `अ६४` and 162 `न६४` after it; the corpus ledger
॰ stood at 559/0/819, sum 1378. **THE LEDGER NOT MOVING IS THE RESULT.**
॰
॰ THE READING IS NEW AND IT IS THE FIRST MADE OFF ONE DECLARATION RATHER
॰ THAN OFF A SIGNATURE PER ROUTINE: *THIS DIVIDER IS NOT THREE ROUTINES
॰ THAT HAPPEN TO AGREE, IT IS ONE EXPRESSION SPLIT INTO THREE, AND A
॰ SINGLE `i64` AT THE TOP OF THE TWIN COLOURS EVERY SITE BELOW IT.*
॰ `encode.rs:1491` writes `let offset = i64::from(*target) - i64::from(base)`
॰ and nothing narrows it after: `:1492`'s `hi` is that offset shifted and
॰ `:1493`'s `value` is `hi` or the offset less `hi` shifted back. Neither
॰ has a signature of its own — they are `let`s — so the sign is decided
॰ ONCE and inherited five times. Every earlier unit read each routine
॰ against its own twin signature; there are none to read here.
॰
॰ AND THE COUNTER-CASE IS INSIDE THE SAME DIVIDER, WHICH IS WHY THE 7 IS A
॰ SUM OF TWO READINGS AND NOT ONE. स्थानाधारः is the third routine here
॰ and its twin (`pc`, `base`) is `u32` on BOTH sides; it is signed only
॰ because T1 has no `न३२` in which `pc.wrapping_sub(4)`'s wrap at 2^32
॰ could be spelled. Two routines signed by the offset they split, one
॰ signed by a width this port does not have.
॰
॰ WHY `न६४` HERE WOULD BE A CORRECTNESS DEFECT AND NOT A STYLE ONE: the
॰ same two lines over the same bits give three different answers at the
॰ three spellings available. `दक्षिणसृ` on a signed value is arithmetic
॰ and on an unsigned one is logical, so a backwards reference — offset
॰ ऋण०षोड्१००० — has उपरिखण्डम् answer ऋण१ signed and something near 2^52
॰ unsigned. The guard demonstrates that rather than asserting it.
॰
॰ THE SECOND RESULT IS WHAT THE ०षोड्८०० IS FOR, AND NOTHING HAD CHECKED
॰ IT. The comment below explains the rounding in prose and nowhere
॰ measures it. The property is TWO claims, not one: the halves reconstruct
॰ the offset, AND the low half always lands inside the signed 12-bit range
॰ the I-format field can hold. A wrong rounding constant keeps the first
॰ and loses the second — which surfaces as an E06 on a line the user did
॰ not write wrong. Checked over thirteen offsets from ऋण२^31 to 2^31-2049.
॰
॰ AND THE PAIR THIS DIVIDER LEAVES OWING, OWED BY A CALLER THAT DOES NOT
॰ EXIST YET. स्थानमूल्यम्'s answer is PLACED: the twin writes
॰ `imm.fits(value as u64)` and `imm.place(value as u64)`, and `fits`
॰ reinterprets with `value as i64` inside itself. ADR-0031 makes the pair
॰ at the CALLER, so when T1 grows this call site it must hand अन्तर्भावः a
॰ न६४ member that स्थानमूल्यम् does not return. Recorded, not discharged.
॰
॰ WHAT THIS UNIT DID NOT TAKE. The 24 `अ६४` left are unchanged from the
॰ part before: the head declarations (6 — CORRECTED 2026-09-03: this
॰ parenthesis named them WRONG. They are the relaxation-round limit, the
॰ three relocation sections and the two record fields; NOT a register
॰ field and NOT लक्ष्य, neither of which is a 64-bit site at all — see
॰ the account above), placing a value into a field (5, of which ONE moves —
॰ विस्तृतिः), the value that half carries (7, ALL SEVEN CORRECT — this unit),
॰ laying out and emitting (3, ALL THREE CORRECT), assembling a word (1)
॰ and what is NOT ported yet (2). **ON SITES THAT ACTUALLY MOVE, THE HEAD
॰ DECLARATIONS ARE NOW THE ONLY UNIT OF ANY SIZE LEFT IN THIS FILE — 6,
॰ against विस्तृतिः's 1, assembling a word's 1 and the two unported.**
॰ They are the file's RECORD TYPES, so taking them puts every section that
॰ reads a field into disagreement at once.
॰
॰ *The account of LAYING OUT AND EMITTING follows and is kept, because its
॰ reading — a divider whose finished state is not 0 — is the one this unit
॰ took to its limit:*
॰
॰ THE PART BEFORE THIS ONE WAS **LAYING OUT AND EMITTING** — the largest single
॰ piece the file had left, and larger than every other divider put together:
॰ the divider ENTIRE bar the one routine whose twin casts to `i64`.
॰ संरेखान्तरम्'s two parameters, its return and its संरेखितम्;
॰ संरेखपूरणाष्टकम्'s three parameters and its four bindings अग्रिमम्,
॰ शिष्टम्, स्थितिः and चतुष्कम्; विन्याससाम्यम्'s दैर्घ्य and सूचकाङ्क; and
॰ पदाष्टकम्'s क्रमः. **14 sites and the census sees all fourteen.**
॰ `encode.t1` carried 38 `अ६४` and 148 `न६४`; it carries 24 and 162 now.
॰ Corpus ledger 573/0/805 -> **559/0/819**, sum still 1378.
॰
॰ THIS DIVIDER DOES NOT REACH 0 AND THAT IS ITS FINISHED STATE, NOT A
॰ SHORTFALL. Three `अ६४` remain — विन्यासविचलनम्'s two parameters and its
॰ return — and they are CORRECT. Every other section this repair finished
॰ reached 0; this one cannot. A later cycle reading the divider as unfinished
॰ from the count alone would respell them, and
॰ `the_alignment_arithmetic_is_unsigned_because_its_differences_are_guarded`
॰ fails if it does.
॰
॰ THE READING IS NEW AND IT IS THE FIRST THAT ADJUDICATES A DIVIDER IN BOTH
॰ DIRECTIONS AT ONCE: *THE TWIN SPELLS THE SIGN OF EVERY DIFFERENCE HERE, AND
॰ IT SPELLS FOUR OF THEM UNSIGNED AND ONE SIGNED — AND WHAT SEPARATES THEM IS
॰ THE GUARD.* This divider is five subtractions in 110 lines, more than any
॰ other section of the file:
॰
॰   संरेखितम् वियोगः क्रमसूचकः        guarded by the यावत् above it
॰   पूरणम् वियोगः अग्रिमम्            guarded by यदि पूरणम् अधिकम् १
॰   क्रमः वियोगः अग्रिमम्             guarded by the early return above it
॰   शिष्टम् वियोगः (शिष्टम् युक् ३)   guarded by the remainder itself
॰   उत्सृष्टम् वियोगः विन्यस्तम्      NOT GUARDED — and it is the one left
॰
॰ The cycle before this one found the first counter-case to this file's
॰ standing rule *a signed quantity in this port is almost always a DIFFERENCE*
॰ and stated the repair as *a guarded difference is not a signed one*. There
॰ it decided ONE site; here it decides a whole unit. And the twin testifies to
॰ BOTH halves rather than one: `align_pad_at` (`encode.rs:1747`) and
॰ `align_fill` (`:1759`) are `u32` from parameter to return and name no signed
॰ type between them, while the drift विन्यासविचलनम् computes is written
॰ `(text.len() as i64 - i64::from(addresses[i]))` at `:637` and `:1067` — an
॰ explicit `i64` cast, and the only signed type this whole divider's twin
॰ names. **So विन्यासविचलनम् is signed BY ITS TWIN and not merely by the
॰ rule**, which is a stronger claim than the one ADR-0031 filed it under.
॰
॰ AND THE UNGUARDED ONE IS UNGUARDED ON PURPOSE. Layout and emission are two
॰ passes and nothing requires them to agree; the encoder checks that they do,
॰ and a check for a disagreement that could go EITHER WAY is exactly where a
॰ sign is earned. The other four are arithmetic whose negative case the code
॰ has already excluded.
॰
॰ THE SECOND RESULT IS THE PADDING OCTETS, AND NOTHING HAD EVER CHECKED THEM.
॰ संरेखपूरणाष्टकम् answers १ and १९ and the comments beside them explain the
॰ numbers in prose; the guard computes them from `0x0001u16.to_le_bytes()` and
॰ `0x0000_0013u32.to_le_bytes()` — the twin's own literals — along with the
॰ २-octet width of the leading c.nop and the ३ mask that follows from `nop`
॰ being four octets wide. A wrong octet here pads `.text` with something that
॰ is not `nop`, which on RISC-V traps, and only the differential oracle
॰ against GNU `as` would ever have noticed.
॰
॰ WHAT THIS UNIT DID NOT TAKE, RE-MEASURED PER DIVIDER WITH THE CENSUS'S OWN
॰ METHOD. The 24 `अ६४` left are: the head declarations (6 — one register
॰ field, three relocation sections, and two under `which instruction set the
॰ image is for`), placing a value into a field (5, of which ONE moves — see
॰ below), the value that half carries (7), laying out and emitting (3, ALL
॰ THREE CORRECT), assembling a word (1) and what is NOT ported yet (2).
॰ **`the value that half carries` is now the largest divider with sites left
॰ to move, and the head declarations — the file's RECORD TYPES — are the
॰ largest unit.**
॰
॰ *The account of THE TWO HALVES OF AN ADDRESS follows and is kept, because
॰ the reading it made is the one this unit generalised:*
॰
॰ THE PART BEFORE THIS ONE WAS **THE TWO HALVES OF AN ADDRESS** — the divider entire,
॰ the first taken by a divider since cycle 529: स्थानप्रत्ययदैर्घ्यम्'s
॰ return, स्थानप्रत्ययाष्टकम्'s क्रमः, and स्थानप्रत्ययवत्'s four bindings
॰ प्रत्ययदैर्घ्य, मूलदैर्घ्य, आरम्भः and सूचकाङ्क. **6 sites and the census
॰ sees all six** — this divider hides no slice element types either, so 0
॰ here is the whole claim. `encode.t1` carried 44 `अ६४` and 142 `न६४`; it
॰ carries 38 and 148 now. Corpus ledger 579/0/799 -> **573/0/805**, sum
॰ still 1378.
॰
॰ THE HANDLE THE LAST CYCLE SAID DID NOT EXIST WAS LEFT BY CYCLE 529 ITSELF,
॰ AND IT IS A DUPLICATED ROUTINE. प्रत्ययवत् (`bytes and words`, remediated
॰ by 529) and स्थानप्रत्ययवत् (this divider) are THE SAME WALK WRITTEN
॰ TWICE — the same four binding names in the same order, the same early
॰ return between them, thirty lines apart in one file — and 529 spelled the
॰ general one `न६४` while leaving the specialised one `अ६४`. No reading had
॰ to be made afresh here: one was already made and only half applied. That
॰ is a fourth shape of handle, after the call-site disagreement (525-527),
॰ the cross-module type (529) and the discriminant family (530, 531).
॰
॰ THE READING IS 529'S OWN AND THIS IS ITS SECOND AND LARGER WITNESS: *THE
॰ TWIN HAS NO NUMBER HERE, AND THE PORT'S NUMBERS ARE THE ONES THE STANDARD
॰ LIBRARY SPELLED FOR IT.* `split_address_part` (`encode.rs:411`) is two
॰ `str::strip_suffix` calls and nothing else; no integer is named anywhere
॰ in it. Every site in this divider exists because T1 has no string type and
॰ had to write the octet walk out by hand, and a `str`'s length and an index
॰ into it are `usize` in every signature `core` gives them.
॰
॰ AND THE ONE SUBTRACTION HERE IS THIS FILE'S COUNTER-CASE TO ITS OWN
॰ STANDING RULE. *A signed quantity in this port is almost always a
॰ DIFFERENCE* has carried four routines to `अ६४` (स्थानाधारः, उपरिखण्डम्,
॰ स्थानमूल्यम्, विन्यासविचलनम्). `आरम्भः भवति मूलदैर्घ्य वियोगः
॰ प्रत्ययदैर्घ्य` is a difference too and it is UNSIGNED, because the routine
॰ returns असत्यम् two lines earlier when the base is shorter than the
॰ suffix. The rule holds where nothing has excluded the negative case; a
॰ GUARDED difference is not a signed one, and the guard is what the test
॰ pins.
॰
॰ WHAT THIS UNIT DID NOT TAKE, RE-MEASURED PER DIVIDER WITH THE CENSUS'S OWN
॰ METHOD. The 38 `अ६४` left are: the head declarations (6 — one register
॰ field, three relocation sections, and two under `which instruction set the
॰ image is for`), placing a value into a field (5), the value that half
॰ carries (7), laying out and emitting (17), assembling a word (1) and what
॰ is NOT ported yet (2). **`laying out and emitting` is still the largest
॰ single piece left, and it is now larger than every other divider put
॰ together.** `the two halves of an address` is at 0 and drops off this
॰ list, as `choosing a compressed form` did last cycle.
॰
॰ AND `placing a value into a field` IS SMALLER THAN ITS 5 SUGGESTS, WHICH
॰ IS THE ONE THING THIS CYCLE READ AND DID NOT SPEND. Four of the five are
॰ CORRECT: `चिह्नितम्` in अन्तर्भावः and in चिह्नितान्तर्भावः is `fits`'s
॰ `let signed = value as i64`, and both `सीमा` are `let limit = 1i64 << …`,
॰ negated on the very next line. Only `विस्तृतिः` moves — `let span = 1u64
॰ << width` at `encode.rs:126`. A cycle picking that divider for its count
॰ would find one site, not five.
॰
॰ `the_address_half_walks_octets_because_its_twin_walks_a_string` pins the
॰ twin's two `strip_suffix` calls, the four bindings in BOTH copies of the
॰ walk, the guard in both, and — the part nothing had ever checked — every
॰ octet of स्थानप्रत्ययाष्टकम्'s table against the real UTF-8 of `ॱउपरि`
॰ and `ॱअधः`. This file's own comment said those numbers were "checked
