॰ THE READING IS THE SLOT KIND'S, AND THIS IS THE SECOND WITNESS TO IT: *A
॰ DISCRIMINANT IS UNSIGNED, AND HERE THE TWIN HAS NO NUMBER TO READ AT ALL.*
॰ `reduce` (`encode.rs:858`) takes `relation: &str` and matches it against
॰ the five string literals `spec/compression-choices.tsv` writes in its
॰ fourth column — `"arg1=arg0"`, `"arg1=zero"`, `"arg2=zero"`, `"arg0=zero"`,
॰ `"none"` — with a `_ => None` arm under them. There is no field, no
॰ parameter and no return in the twin whose sign could be read. The integer
॰ exists ONLY because T1 has no string-equality operator, and this section's
॰ own comment has said exactly that since the port was written.
॰
॰ AND THE ONE THING THAT DISTINGUISHES THIS FAMILY FROM THE SLOT KINDS IS ITS
॰ ०, WHICH THE SLOT-KIND UNIT ASKED THE NEXT CYCLE TO SETTLE OUT LOUD.
॰ `असम्बन्धः भवति ०` is glossed *a relation this reader does not model*, and
॰ its twin is `reduce`'s `_ => None` — the arm for a fourth column this port
॰ does not know. The slot kinds have no ० because a slot always HAS a kind;
॰ the relations have one because the TABLE is data on disk and may name a
॰ relation the reader was not written for. **NEITHER FACT IS A SIGN.** ० is
॰ the smallest value either family spells, `सम्बन्धः` is only ever compared
॰ with `समम्`, and nothing in this file subtracts from it or negates it. An
॰ absent-marker is a value the enumeration reserves, not a negative one, and
॰ this file says so itself twenty lines below: `मध्यरूप and व्याकर already
॰ settled this collision the same way, by counting from १ and letting ० mean
॰ ABSENT`. Both of those modules — `ir.t1` and `parse.t1` — are remediated
॰ entire and hold **zero** `अ६४` between them, so the shape they settled it
॰ into is `न६४`.
॰
॰ THE TWO `अ६४` THIS DIVIDER STILL HOLDS ARE CORRECT AND MUST NOT BE
॰ "REMEDIATED" — THEY ARE THE FIRST SITES OF THIS FILE'S UNSIGNED DIRECTION
॰ EXAMINED AND DELIBERATELY LEFT. `मूल्यानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ६४` in
॰ अपाकर्तव्यम् (`:1496`) and in सङ्कोचनिषेधः (`:1571`) is
॰ `values: &[(&str, i64)]` — `Decoded::operands`, SIGNED at
॰ `vishlesana.rs:50` and settled there by cycle 514 — and अपाकर्तव्यम्
॰ compares those values with each other and with ० to decide whether an
॰ operand repeats. The census cannot see either site, so neither is in the
॰ 44 above and neither ever was in the 1322: a slice declares `अङ्कः` after
॰ `ॱॱ` and hides its element type two words further on. **A later cycle
॰ reading this divider as "0 left" from the ledger alone would find two `अ६४`
॰ here and could only conclude they were missed.** They were not.
॰
॰ THE DEFERRAL THIS DISCHARGES IS THE LAST ONE ITEM 4 HELD. `सम्बन्धः ॱॱ अ६४`
॰ was the single surviving entry of
॰ `the_signed_half_of_encode_t1_is_what_adr_0031_names`, kept since cycle 524
॰ under *a kind moves with its siblings*; its siblings are in this unit, so
॰ the entry is **DELETED rather than edited**, as its own message instructed,
॰ and with it the single-element binding that clippy's
॰ `single_element_loop` had already forced out of a `for`. That list is now
॰ empty. Item 6 of the slot-kind guard — the border assertion — is deleted
॰ the same way and for the same reason.
