॰ *The account of THE SLOT KIND follows and is kept, because the bound it
॰ stated is still the bound on the sites it did not take:*
॰
॰ THE PART CYCLE 530 TOOK WAS **THE SLOT KIND** — not a divider but a
॰ FAMILY, taken wherever this file spells it: the seven constants कोष्ठभेद … अन्तरभेद, the
॰ अवकाश ॱ भेद field that holds one, the four parameters of the three
॰ predicates that read one (कोष्ठवाचकः, तत्कालवाचकः, समानभेदः twice), the two
॰ भेदाः slices (पदरचना, अपाकर्तव्यम्) and the one binding drawn from a slice
॰ (लिखितभेदः). **15 sites, of which the census sees 13.** `encode.t1` carried
॰ 64 `अ६४` and 122 `न६४`; it carries 51 and 135 now. Corpus ledger
॰ 599/0/779 -> **586/0/792**, sum still 1378.
॰
॰ AND THIS IS THE FIRST UNIT IN THIS FILE WHOSE FILE COUNT AND LEDGER MOVE BY
॰ DIFFERENT NUMBERS, WHICH IS WHY THE BOUND IS STATED IN SITES AND NOT IN
॰ SITES-THE-CENSUS-SEES. The census counts the token after `ॱॱ` or `ददाति`;
॰ where a slice is declared that token is `अङ्कः` and the element type is two
॰ words further on, so `भेदाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ६४` in पदरचना (`:1239`) and in
॰ अपाकर्तव्यम् (`:1311`) are repaired and move NOTHING. `vishlesana.t1` hit
॰ this first — its अवकाशमूल्यानि and अवकाशभेदाः are the two the ledger comment
॰ already names — and the lesson is the same one: a cycle that repaired only
॰ what the ledger can see would leave a slice disagreeing with the element
॰ type it is filled from.
॰
॰ THE READING IS *A DISCRIMINANT IS UNSIGNED, AND HERE THE TWIN HAS NO NUMBER
॰ TO READ AT ALL* — the strongest form of the case cycle 529 met once. The
॰ slot kind is a STRING in Rust: `encode.rs` writes `reg`, `freg`, `imm`,
॰ `simm`, `label`, `fixed` and `disp` and compares them with `==`, so there
॰ is no field, no parameter and no return whose sign could be read. The
॰ integer exists ONLY because T1 has no string-equality operator yet, which
॰ the constants' own block comment has said since the port was written. What
॰ the port chose is therefore all there is to read, and it is legible: seven
॰ values numbered from १, no ० — a slot always HAS a kind — and `भेद` is
॰ never arithmetic anywhere in the corpus, only `समम्` and `असमम्`. There is
॰ no negative for it to spell and nothing to subtract it from.
॰
॰ THE SIBLINGS HAD ALREADY MOVED — IN FIVE OTHER FILES AND, WORSE, IN TWO OF
॰ THIS FILE'S OWN CONSUMERS. Every other `*भेद` discriminant family in the
॰ corpus is `न६४` already: `artha.t1`'s twelve `Ty` kinds (`:103`-`:114`),
॰ `ast.t1`'s five type, thirteen operator, eight expression and eight
॰ statement kinds, `ir.t1`'s five instruction and three terminator kinds,
॰ `lex.t1`'s eight token kinds, `parse.t1`'s three declaration kinds and
॰ `utsarjana.t1`'s two location kinds. The ONLY other family still `अ६४` is
॰ `vakyavibhaga.t1`'s, and that file is unremediated entire.
॰
॰ AND THE MIRROR OF THIS ONE WAS ALREADY WRITTEN IN `न६४`, THREE TIMES, IN
॰ TWO REMEDIATED MODULES. `vishlesana.t1:113` declares
॰ `भेद ॱॱ न६४` and glosses it *the slot kind, in सङ्केतन's numbering — a
॰ discriminant*; `चिह्नितावकाशः` (`:135`) takes `भेद ॱॱ न६४` and compares it
॰ to THIS file's `सङ्केतनॱअन्तरभेद` and `सङ्केतनॱसचिह्नतत्कालभेद`;
॰ `अवकाशभेदाः` (`:239`) takes `भेदाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः न६४`; and
॰ `samyojana.t1`'s `पूरणीयावकाशः` (`:497`) takes `भेदः ॱॱ न६४` and compares it
॰ to `सङ्केतनॱतत्कालभेद`. So the file that OWNS the constants was the one
॰ disagreeing with them. That is the class cycle 529 found in `भाषा`/
॰ `Language` — an unremediated declarer read by a remediated consumer — and
॰ this is the THIRD instance and by far the largest, being a whole family
॰ rather than one parameter.
॰
॰ THE DEFERRAL THIS DISCHARGES, AND THE ONE IT DOES NOT. Item 4 of
॰ `the_signed_half_of_encode_t1_is_what_adr_0031_names` held two entries;
॰ `भेदाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ६४` is **DELETED from that list rather than edited**,
॰ as its own message instructs. `सम्बन्धः ॱॱ अ६४` STAYS, and the reason is now
॰ sharper than *its siblings are outside every unit taken so far*: its six
॰ siblings असम्बन्धः … प्रथमशून्यसम्बन्धः are INSIDE this file, at `:1294`-
॰ `:1299`, under `choosing a compressed form`, a divider this unit does not
॰ cross. They are also a different family in a way worth writing down — one
॰ of them is `भवति ०`, *a relation this reader does not know*, where the slot
॰ kinds have no ० at all. Neither is −१, so neither earns a sign; but they
॰ move as two families and not one.
॰
॰ WHAT THIS UNIT DID NOT TAKE, RE-MEASURED PER DIVIDER. The 51 `अ६४` left
॰ are: the head declarations (6 — one register field, three relocation
॰ sections, प्रतीक्षा ॱ कोष्ठकम् and सङ्केतनदोष ॱ पङ्क्ति), placing a value
॰ into a field (5), the two halves of an address (6), the value that half
॰ carries (7), laying out and emitting (17), assembling a word (1),
॰ choosing a compressed form (7) and what is NOT ported yet (2). **`laying
॰ out and emitting` is still the largest single piece left.** The slot-kind
