॰ THE PART CYCLE 529 TOOK WAS **BYTES-AND-WORDS TOGETHER WITH
॰ DIAGNOSTICS** — the two
॰ smallest remaining sections, taken as ONE unit because they share one
॰ reading: प्रत्ययवत्, चतुरष्टकम्, चतुरष्टकसंख्या and सङ्केतनदोषवचनम्.
॰ 7 sites and the census sees all seven: the unit wraps no 64-bit type in
॰ `अङ्कः अन्तः`, `सम्भाव्य` or `दोषयुक्त`, so the file's count and the ledger
॰ move together. `encode.t1` carried 71 `अ६४` and 115 `न६४`; it carried 64
॰ and 122 after. Corpus ledger 606/0/772 -> **599/0/779**, sum still 1378.
॰ THE FILE IS STILL NOT REMEDIATED: 64 `अ६४` remain and the sections holding
॰ them are named at the foot of this account.
॰
॰ THE READING IS *THE TWIN HAS NO NUMBER HERE, AND THE PORT'S NUMBERS ARE THE
॰ ONES THE STANDARD LIBRARY SPELLED FOR IT.* This is the first unit in this
॰ file whose sites exist because of what Rust HIDES rather than because of
॰ what it declares. `split_address_part` (`encode.rs:411`) writes
॰ `base.strip_suffix("ॱउपरि")` and `words` (`:711`) writes
॰ `text.chunks_exact(4)`; neither names an integer type at all, and the three
॰ that stand behind them — `str::strip_suffix`'s comparison, `chunks_exact`'s
॰ stride and the `Vec<u32>::len` that `चतुरष्टकसंख्या` answers with — are
॰ `usize` in every signature `core` gives them. T1 has none of the three, so
॰ the port writes the walk out by hand, and every site it writes is a LENGTH
॰ (`मूलदैर्घ्य`, `प्रत्ययदैर्घ्य`), an INDEX (`सूचकाङ्क`, `स्थानम्`) or a
॰ COUNT (`दैर्घ्य विभाजनम् ४`).
॰
॰ THE ONE SUBTRACTION IS GUARDED BY THE COMPARISON DIRECTLY ABOVE IT, WHICH
॰ IS WHY IT IS NOT A DIFFERENCE. `आरम्भः भवति मूलदैर्घ्य वियोगः
॰ प्रत्ययदैर्घ्य` cannot go below ० because
॰ `यदि मूलदैर्घ्य न्यूनम् प्रत्ययदैर्घ्य` has already returned असत्यम् on
॰ exactly that case — the same shape `स्थानप्रत्ययवत्` repeats further down.
॰ `a_negative_sentinel_is_what_keeps_a_site_signed` asks for a negative the
॰ file could produce; a guarded subtraction produces none.
॰
॰ AND THE SEVENTH SITE IS AN ENUM DISCRIMINANT WHOSE SIBLINGS ARE ALREADY
॰ REMEDIATED — IN ANOTHER FILE. `सङ्केतनदोषवचनम्`'s `भाषा` is
॰ `EncodeError::message(&self, lang: Language)` (`encode.rs:392`), and
॰ `Language` is ported in `nidana.t1`, which was remediated long ago:
॰ `संस्कृतभाषा` and `आङ्ग्लभाषा` are `न६४` at `nidana.t1:688`-`:689`, and both
॰ `विवरणम्` (`:864`) and `सन्देश` (`:913`) take `भाषा ॱॱ न६४`. So this was a
॰ live CROSS-MODULE DISAGREEMENT and not a discriminant awaiting its
॰ siblings: the rule cycle 524 stated for `भेदाः` and `सम्बन्धः` — *a kind
॰ moves with its siblings* — SETTLES this one rather than defers it, because
॰ the siblings have already moved. It is the only discriminant in this file
॰ whose siblings live elsewhere.
॰
॰ ONE STALE COMMENT FIXED IN PLACE, NO ROW FILED. `प्रत्ययवत्`'s header said
॰ *"the test स्थानभागः rests on"*; `स्थानभागः` (`:1690` before this edit)
॰ rests on `स्थानप्रत्ययवत्` instead, which walks the octets
