॰ ══ slot kinds ══
॰ Rust writes these as the strings `reg`, `freg`, `imm`, `simm`, `label`,
॰ `fixed` and `disp`. T1 has no string-equality operator yet, so the kind is
॰ an integer here and the table reader maps the column onto it.
॰ ADR-0031, TASK `D-002h`: THESE ARE `न६४` AND THE TWIN HAS NO NUMBER HERE
॰ AT ALL. `encode.rs` compares the strings above with `==`; there is no field
॰ whose sign could be read, and the integer exists only because of the line
॰ directly above this one. Seven values numbered from १, no ० — a slot always
॰ HAS a kind — and `भेद` is compared and never added to anywhere in the
॰ corpus. `vishlesana.t1:113` and `samyojana.t1:497` had ALREADY spelled this
॰ same discriminant `न६४`, so until this cycle the file that owns the
॰ constants was the one disagreeing with its own readers.
सार्वजनिक चरः कोष्ठभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।          ॰ reg
सार्वजनिक चरः प्लवकोष्ठभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।       ॰ freg
सार्वजनिक चरः तत्कालभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।         ॰ imm
सार्वजनिक चरः सचिह्नतत्कालभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।    ॰ simm
सार्वजनिक चरः नामाङ्कभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।         ॰ label
सार्वजनिक चरः स्थिरभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ६ ।           ॰ fixed
सार्वजनिक चरः अन्तरभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ७ ।           ॰ disp

॰ ══ which section a relocation offset counts from ══
॰ mirrors कोश ॱ RelSection — Text, Data, Debug(name).
सार्वजनिक चरः पाठकोष्ठकम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।        ॰ RelSection::Text
सार्वजनिक चरः दत्तकोष्ठकम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।       ॰ RelSection::Data
सार्वजनिक चरः शोधनकोष्ठकम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।       ॰ RelSection::Debug

॰ ══ which instruction set the image is for ══
सार्वजनिक गणना लक्ष्य आरभ्य ॰ Target
  असङ्कुचितम् ऽ ॰ Uncompressed — every instruction is 32 bits. The default.
  सङ्कुचितम्    ॰ Compressed — choose a 16-bit form wherever the assembler would.
समाप्तम् ।

॰ one `(value bit, encoding bit)` pair of a slot's derived map.
॰ Rust writes this as the tuple `(u32, u32)`; T1 has no tuple type, so the
॰ pair is a struct and `न्यास` below is a slice of it.
सार्वजनिक संरचना अंशयुग्म आरभ्य
  मूलांश ॱॱ अ३२ ऽ    ॰ the bit of the value
  सङ्केतांश ॱॱ अ३२   ॰ the bit of the encoding it goes to
समाप्तम् ।

॰ one operand slot of one encoding — Slot.
सार्वजनिक संरचना अवकाश आरभ्य
  भेद ॱॱ न६४ ऽ                    ॰ kind: reg, freg, imm, label or fixed
  आवरण ॱॱ अ३२ ऽ                   ॰ mask: which encoding bits this slot occupies
  न्यास ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अंशयुग्म ऽ    ॰ map: (value bit, encoding bit) pairs
  आधार ॱॱ अ३२                     ॰ bias: the lowest value the field accepts
समाप्तम् ।

॰ W-247 (2026-09-04): `संरचना प्रतीक्षा` STOOD HERE TOO — five fields (नाम, भेद,
॰ स्थान, कोष्ठकम्, कोष्ठकनाम), the first port of Rust's `Pending` — and forty
॰ lines below a second `संरचना प्रतीक्षा` with two. The parser accepted both,
॰ the loader kept the last, and no pass said which was meant. THE CODE MEANS
॰ THE SECOND: `प्रतीक्षायोजनम्` fills `नाम` and `स्थानम्` and nothing in the
॰ corpus builds or reads the five (found by W-223's store: the corpus's one
॰ duplicate declaration). This one is gone; the survivor's margin says what
॰ of `Pending` it does not yet carry.

॰ one entry of the symbol table — one pair of Rust's `BTreeMap<String, u32>`.
॰
॰ THE SECOND OF THE TWO SIGNATURE DEBTS `स्थानसङ्केतनम्` RECORDED, PAID
॰ 2026-08-31. That margin said Rust's third argument "has no parameter at
॰ all" and that the divergence was "a real one to decide, not a typo: a
॰ `BTreeMap<String, u32>` becomes an arena and a linear search, the shape
॰ `संज्ञाप्रविष्टि` already uses in artha.t1". This is that decision taken.
॰ The map has two readers inside encode_collecting — a label's address and
॰ the address a `ॱउपरि`/`ॱअधः` half is measured against — and both are
॰ `get`, so a search is the whole of what the shape has to support.
॰
॰ ZERO-BASED, and that is not this file's usual convention. Every arena in
॰ `वाक्यविभाग` is one-based because a `…योजनम्` returns the index it wrote
॰ at and ० has to mean ABSENT there. Nothing appends to this one: a caller
॰ builds it whole and hands it over, exactly as `सङ्केत ॱ अवकाशाः` is built
॰ whole by `पङ्क्तिसङ्केतः` and is zero-based for the same reason. An arena
॰ is born holding one शून्यम्, so an EMPTY table is one slot holding
॰ शून्यम् — which is Rust's `&BTreeMap::new()`, what `सङ्केतनम्` passes —
॰ and `चिह्नस्थानम्` asks that of every entry before reading it.
सार्वजनिक संरचना चिह्नस्थान आरभ्य
  नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ           ॰ the label
  स्थान ॱॱ अ३२                     ॰ the address it stands at
समाप्तम् ।

॰ a name this object could not resolve — Pending, encode.rs:172.
॰
॰ An OBJECT may reference a name it does not define; that is what a linker is
॰ for. An EXECUTABLE may not, and `स्थानसङ्केतनम्` refuses one with E05 at two
॰ sites. Rust threads `Option<&mut Vec<Pending>>` to tell those apart. T1 has no
॰ such argument, and the owner ruled on 2026-08-31 that this is module state and
॰ a flag rather than a third change to `स्थानसङ्केतनम्`'s signature — two rows
॰ had already settled it.
॰ THE ONE `प्रतीक्षा` (W-247): Rust's `Pending` carries `name`, `kind` (a relocation
॰ type from spec/relocations-riscv64.tsv), `at` and `section`; the T1 assembler
॰ records the name and the offset, because its two E05 sites patch nothing yet —
॰ `kind` and `section` are the linker side's to add when `संयोजन` reads this
॰ arena, and that is a row, not a second declaration.
सार्वजनिक संरचना प्रतीक्षा आरभ्य
  नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ           ॰ the name that was not defined here
  स्थानम् ॱॱ अ३२ ऽ                  ॰ the octet offset of the field to patch
  भेदः ॱॱ अ३२ ऽ                     ॰ WHICH relocation applies — spec/relocations-riscv64.tsv
  कोष्ठकम् ॱॱ न६४                   ॰ the section that offset counts from
समाप्तम् ।

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ `भेदः` AND `कोष्ठकम्` ARE W-247's DEFERRAL, COLLECTED ON SCHEDULE.
॰
॰ The margin above this record has read, since 2026-09-04: "the T1 assembler
॰ records the name and the offset, because its two E05 sites patch nothing yet
॰ — `kind` and `section` are the linker side's to add WHEN `संयोजन` READS THIS
॰ ARENA, and that is a row, not a second declaration." That moment is now: the
॰ object builder below turns this arena into `वास्तुॱपुनःस्थापनम्` records, and
॰ a relocation without its type is a patch without a rule.
॰
॰ A DELIBERATE DEFERRAL COLLECTED ON SCHEDULE IS NOT A GAP DISCOVERED. The
॰ arena was built two-thirds of the way on purpose and the remaining third was
॰ left to whoever first needed it.
॰
॰ AND THIS IS THE ONE DECISION IN THIS PATH RUST MAKES AND `.t1` DID NOT.
॰ Everything else the builder does is bookkeeping over things already
॰ computed; CHOOSING THE RELOCATION FOR AN INSTRUCTION FORM is a compiler
॰ decision, and while it lived only in `encode.rs` the chain could not be said
॰ to compile without Rust however well the rest ran.
॰
॰ THE NUMBERS MIRROR `spec/relocations-riscv64.tsv` AND ARE GUARDED, NOT
॰ TRUSTED. `संयोजन ॱ भेदाङ्कः` reads that file at run time and answers the
॰ number for a name; `t1_vastu_build.rs` asserts each constant below EQUALS
॰ what it answers. A mirror nothing checks is a hardcode that drifts in
॰ silence — this file mirrors `स्थापन` and `RelSection` the same way and for
॰ the same stated reason, and neither of those is checked yet.
