॰ WHETHER a decimal field is there — the question दशाङ्कमूल्यम्'s ANSWER
॰ CANNOT CARRY, and the only definition in this file of what a decimal digit
॰ is.
॰
॰ `सम्भाव्य` is ONE WORD and ० means ABSENT — `ir.t1` decides that layout for
॰ kind ५ and its own margin names this as the cost. So a caller that asks
॰ `यदि मूल्यम् असमम् शून्यम्` is asking about the PAYLOAD WORD, and for a
॰ field whose ० is an ordinary value — a bit number, a register number, a
॰ domain bit — the answer is PRESENT interpreted and ABSENT in the image.
॰ MEASURED 2026-09-19: `शून्यविकल्पपरीक्षा` answers ७००१ interpreted and ७००२
॰ natively, and `विश्लेषणॱन्यासरचना` dropped 484 of the encoding table's 2801
॰ pairs on exactly that divergence.
॰
॰ WHETHER a decimal field is present is a property of the TEXT and not of the
॰ number read out of it, so it is asked of the text. This answers असत्यम् for
॰ exactly the two ranges दशाङ्कमूल्यम् answers शून्यम् for — an empty range,
॰ and a range holding an octet outside ४८…५७ — and सत्यम् otherwise, `0`
॰ INCLUDED. It does not repair kind ५'s representation and does not claim to:
॰ it lets a caller stop depending on it.
