॰ ADR-0030, `D-002h`: THIS DIVIDER IS REMEDIATED ENTIRE — 6 sites, 0
॰ `अ६४` left and none hidden in a slice element type. The reading is at
॰ the head of this file and in
॰ `the_address_half_walks_octets_because_its_twin_walks_a_string`.
॰
॰ `लक्ष्यॱउपरि` is the high 20 bits of the distance to लक्ष्य and
॰ `लक्ष्यॱअधः` the low 12 — how a 32-bit address is built out of two
॰ instructions that each hold less (B-064). Both are PC-RELATIVE and that
॰ is forced rather than chosen: the image loads at 0x80000000, `lui`
॰ sign-extends its immediate, and 0x80000000 sign-extends past the top of
॰ the address space.
॰
॰ RUST STRIPS THESE WITH `strip_suffix("ॱउपरि")` AND T1 HAS NO STRING
॰ LITERAL — `spec/grammar-t1.ebnf`'s frozen `token` production is
॰ keyword | type_name | identifier | numeral | comment, and its own note
॰ says a T1 front end therefore cannot lex one. That is F-004f2 and it is
॰ an ADR, not an edit.
॰
॰ IT IS NOT A BLOCKER HERE, and saying so is the point of this section.
॰ The suffix is needed as OCTETS, not as text: the operand base is already
॰ a byte slice, and `strip_suffix` is a comparison against fifteen known
॰ numbers. स्थानप्रत्ययाष्टकम् below supplies them from numerals, which
॰ the frozen production does list. A string type would make this shorter;
॰ it was never what the comparison needed.
॰ These are the UTF-8 octets of `ॱउपरि` and `ॱअधः`, and each is written
॰ beside the akṣara it spells so the two can be checked against each other
॰ by eye rather than trusted.

॰ how many octets one address modifier spells.
