॰ ══════════════════ the value that half carries ══════════════════
॰
॰ ADR-0030, `D-002h`: THIS DIVIDER IS ADJUDICATED ENTIRE AND NOT ONE SITE
॰ MOVES — 7 `अ६४`, the census sees all seven, and all seven are CORRECT.
॰ 7 IS ITS FINISHED STATE. It is the first divider of this repair that is
॰ finished at its FULL count; every other reached 0, and `laying out and
॰ emitting` reached 3 of 17. A cycle reading the header's per-divider table
॰ alone would take the largest number left and respell every one of them,
॰ and `the_pc_relative_halves_are_signed_because_the_offset_they_split_is`
॰ is what stops that being a silent change.
॰
॰ THE FIVE BELOW स्थानाधारः ARE ONE EXPRESSION SPLIT INTO THREE ROUTINES,
॰ AND THEY INHERIT THEIR SIGN FROM ONE `let`. `encode.rs:1491` declares
॰ `let offset = i64::from(*target) - i64::from(base)`; `hi` and `value` are
॰ derived from it and declare nothing. `दक्षिणसृ` on a signed value is an
॰ arithmetic shift and on an unsigned one is logical, so at `न६४` a
॰ backwards reference would take the high half near 2^52 instead of ऋण१.
॰

॰ the address the half is measured from — Rust's
॰ `if upper { pc } else { pc.wrapping_sub(4) }`.
॰ `ॱअधः` measures from the PRECEDING instruction, because that is the
॰ `auipc` whose register it is completing. GNU spells the same thing
॰ `%pcrel_lo(1b)`, naming the auipc by a back-reference; here the
॰ convention is positional and the two must be adjacent.
॰ ADR-0030, TASK `D-002h`: SIGNED — BUT NOT AS A DIFFERENCE, WHICH IS WHAT
॰ `.loop/STATE.md` HAD PRE-JUDGED IT. The twin is unsigned on BOTH sides:
॰ `encode.rs:533` declares `let mut pc = 0u32` and `:1490` writes `let base = if
॰ upper { pc } else { pc.wrapping_sub(4) }`. This is an ADDRESS, not the
॰ difference computed from one — its two neighbours उपरिखण्डम् and स्थानमूल्यम्
॰ take `offset`, which `:1491` really does declare `i64`.
॰ IT STAYS SIGNED FOR A DIFFERENT REASON, AND THE REASON IS THAT T1 HAS NO
॰ `न३२` IN WHICH THE TWIN'S WRAP COULD BE SPELLED. `pc.wrapping_sub(4)` wraps
॰ at 2^32; an `न६४` here would wrap at 2^64 and an `अ६४` gives ऋण४ — three
॰ different answers, and only the first is the twin's. The port already chose to
॰ widen, and `:1491` widens `base` with `i64::from` before subtracting, so the
॰ signed reading is the one the ONLY consumer of this result uses. ADR-0031's
॰ rule decides it: the caller is where both readings exist, and this port's
॰ caller has already picked. NOTHING CALLS स्थानाधारः IN T1 YET, so the choice
॰ is recorded rather than exercised — and it is recorded because the next reader
॰ would otherwise inherit *"it is a difference"*, which is false.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्थानाधारः आदाय क्रमसूचकः ॱॱ अ६४ उपरि ॱॱ बूल ददाति अ६४ आदि
    यदि उपरि समम् सत्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् क्रमसूचकः ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् क्रमसूचकः वियोगः ४ ।
इति

॰ the high twenty bits, rounded so the low twelve can be signed —
॰ `(offset + 0x800) >> 12`.
॰ the ०षोड्८०० is not a fudge: the low half is sign-extended by the
॰ hardware, so a low half at or past 0x800 reads as negative and the high
॰ half has to have counted one more.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः उपरिखण्डम् आदाय अन्तरम् ॱॱ अ६४ ददाति अ६४ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् आरभ्य अन्तरम् योगः ०षोड्८०० समाप्तम् दक्षिणसृ १२ ।
इति

॰ what goes in the field for the half that was written —
॰ `if upper { hi } else { offset - (hi << 12) }`.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्थानमूल्यम् आदाय अन्तरम् ॱॱ अ६४ उपरि ॱॱ बूल ददाति अ६४ आदि
    चरः उच्चम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति उपरिखण्डम् अन्तरम् ।
    यदि उपरि समम् सत्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् उच्चम् ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् अन्तरम् वियोगः आरभ्य उच्चम् वामसृ १२ समाप्तम् ।
इति


