॰ whether relaxation has settled — Rust's `addresses == previous`, the
॰ test that ends the fixpoint B-007 built.
॰ A DIFFERENT LENGTH IS A DIFFERENT LAYOUT, which is why the lengths are
॰ compared first rather than the common prefix walked: the first round
॰ compares against an empty पूर्वाणि and must not report agreement.
॰ ॥ विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् / विन्यासमुद्रणम् ॥ THE TWO LAYOUTS, OUT THROUGH THE
॰ CHANNEL — the clause-nine instrument, and it instruments the ORIGINAL.
॰
॰ WHY NOT A RUNG. Rungs 74, 76, 77, 77b and 77c each replicated
॰ `लक्ष्यवस्तुसङ्केतनम्`'s prefix and asked one question through a 16-bit status.
॰ Rung 76 spent an entire image to learn one bit — that the two lengths agree.
॰ Three of the replicas failed to reproduce E22 at all, each for a different
॰ faithfulness gap, and the last carries a step of unknown status (a
॰ cross-module WRITE, where rung 78 measured only cross-module READS good).
॰ **The ladder was long because the channel was sixteen bits wide, and it is
॰ not sixteen bits wide any more.** A replica's value rests entirely on its
॰ faithfulness, which is the one property none of them could establish.
॰
॰ So this writes the ACTUAL LOCALS of the actual routine, on the path rung 73
॰ already drives to a faithful `१००३`. The faithfulness question does not get
॰ managed, it disappears — and so does the reset problem, because the original
॰ does its own reset.
॰
॰ OFF BY DEFAULT, AND THE FLAG IS THE WHOLE SAFETY ARGUMENT. Reading state from
॰ inside a path that is mid-refusal can perturb what it measures. `असत्यम्`
॰ means not one octet is written and not one extra call is made, so every
॰ existing reading stands unchanged. The check that it stays honest is stated
॰ where the dump is: the instrumented path must still answer `१००३`.
॰
॰ LENGTH FIRST, THEN ELEMENTS, ALL LITTLE-ENDIAN FOUR OCTETS — `kosha.t1`'s
॰ `प्रतिबिम्बचतुरष्टकम्` is where that order is written down (low half first).
॰ The length prefix is not decoration: the channel is UNFRAMED, so two arrays
॰ in one stream have no boundary, and a run that dies part way leaves a prefix
॰ that reads as a shorter array. With the count in front, a reader knows how
॰ many elements to expect and a short stream names itself instead of looking
॰ like a difference. A diff offset then divides by four into an element index.
सार्वजनिक चरः विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।

॰ THE SWITCH IS A ROUTINE, NOT A GLOBAL A CALLER WRITES. Natively there is no
॰ Rust to reach in and set a flag, so an instrument switched by an external
॰ write is an instrument that only works under the interpreter — which is the
॰ half that already agrees. This is a cross-module CALL whose write is
॰ same-module inside the callee, so it needs nothing rung 78 did not measure.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः विन्यासमुद्रणारम्भः आदाय अर्हम् ॱॱ बूल ददाति न६४ आदि
    विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् भवति अर्हम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

॰ **THE DIVISION OPERATOR IS `विभाजनम्`. `भागः` IS NOT AN OPERATOR AT ALL** —
॰ measured 2026-09-14 by an 8-way bisect over three variables (parameter type,
॰ division token, argument shape) in an isolated corpus copy. The division token
॰ DECIDES alone: `भागः` refuses in all four combinations, `विभाजनम्` compiles in
॰ all four. Parameter type and argument shape decide nothing.
॰
॰ **AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS MARGIN BLAMED THE ARGUMENT SHAPE** — "a bare
॰ expression after a routine name does not become one argument, the CALL binds
॰ first" — citing `kosha.t1:78-81`. That rule is real for `आरभ्य`, and it is NOT
॰ what refused here: the bare-expression form compiles clean. Three things were
॰ changed in one edit and the cause was assigned to the one a margin made
॰ plausible.
॰
॰ **AND THE GREP THAT `REFUTED` `भागः` COUNTED MARGINS.** `grep -c भागः
॰ encode.t1` answers 12, which read as "it exists, so it is not the problem".
॰ Strip the `॰` margins and it is 3, every one the compound `स्थानभागः`. Across
॰ the corpus the standalone token appears only as a LOCAL VARIABLE NAME
॰ (`utsarjana.t1:1062`, `चरः भागः ॱॱ इ६४ भवति ... विभाजनम् १० ...`) — where the
॰ real operator sits on the same line.
॰
॰ The refusal is `अर्थ` exit २ with `अलिखितप्रकारसंख्या १` and **no line, no name
॰ and no construct**, which is why a wrong cause survived this long.
वृत्तिः चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् आदाय मूल्यम् ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः शेषम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति मूल्यम् ।
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् ४ आदि
        चरः अष्टकम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति शेषम् शेषः २५६ ।
        चरः अवगणना ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् अष्टकम् ।
        शेषम् भवति शेषम् विभाजनम् २५६ ।
        क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

॰ A RUN OF OCTETS, SAME FRAME. `सङ्केताङ्क` is the code TEXT — `सङ्केतनकूटः` maps
॰ a number to `E22`, `E23`, `E00` — not a number, so a word writer refuses it:
॰ "expected a number, found Octets([69, 48, 48])", which is `E00`, the sentinel.
॰ Each octet goes out as its own four-octet word so one decoder reads every item.
