॰ where the क्रमः-th candidate row begins, ONE-BASED and counted from ०;
॰ ० when there is no such candidate. `कोष्ठपङ्क्तिः`'s convention, for
॰ `कोष्ठपङ्क्तिः`'s reason: the first row begins at offset ० and ० is
॰ also the answer for "no such row".
॰
॰ FILE ORDER IS THE ORDER, and that is Rust's and not a convenience.
॰ encode.rs:1251 records that 30 families are ambiguous here and that
॰ FILE ORDER decides among them until `B-056` names them apart; a walk
॰ that reordered the candidates would change which encoding those 30
॰ families get.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः कुलसङ्केतपङ्क्तिः आदाय कुलम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ अंशाः ॱॱ अ६४ क्रमः ॱॱ अ६४ ददाति अ६४ आदि
