॰ how many slots this encoding really has — Rust's `e.slots.len()`.
॰ NOT `अवकाशाः ॱ दैर्घ्य`, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS ONE ROW SHAPE. The arena
॰ is zero-based and `पङ्क्तिसङ्केतः` fills it from ०, but an arena is BORN
॰ holding one शून्यम् — so a row with no operand at all, which is what
॰ `(none)` in field ६ spells, reports दैर्घ्य १ and entry ० is not a slot.
॰ `ecall` and `ebreak` are those rows. Every walk over अवकाशाः must ask
॰ this; the three that were written before encode_collecting had a caller
॰ ask ॱ दैर्घ्य and would read a शून्यम् as a slot.
