॰ BLOCKER (c) IS CLOSED — 2026-08-30. Its three clauses were `कोष्ठाङ्कः`,
॰ `क्षेत्रसमूहः` and `sanskrit_text::numeral::bits`; the first two were
॰ already written above and the third landed in `अक्षरकोश` the same day, as
॰ the pair `अंशदोषः`/`अंशाः` (sanskrit_text.t1:451 and :473). NOTHING ELSE
॰ WAS NEEDED. The recorded blocker had also named a split, a bitwise OR and
॰ a bitwise NOT, and the audit above was right that none of the three is
॰ here: the reader takes the WHOLE base, the three clauses are a chain of
॰ early returns rather than a disjunction, and `wrapping_neg` lives inside
॰ `अंशाः` where it is a subtraction from ०.
