॰ ADR-0030, D-002h, MERGED 2026-09-03: this routine answers `सम्भाव्य न६४`
॰ — the rail's spelling, read off `value_of(..) -> Option<u64>`
॰ (encode.rs:439). The rail's side of this merge was still the stub
॰ (`अपूर्णम्`, awaiting (c)); this side's body is kept and only the spelling
॰ moves. `समूहः` moves with it, because its producer `क्षेत्रसमूहः` (:2511)
॰ already answers `सम्भाव्य न६४`. `कोष्ठम्` does NOT: `कोष्ठाङ्कः` (:2311)
॰ answers `सम्भाव्य अ३२` and that boundary is not this merge's to move.
॰
॰ THE ORDER OF THE THREE IS LOAD-BEARING and is Rust's. A register name is
॰ asked first, so a table that ever named a register `१०` would still answer
॰ its number and not the numeral. A domain set is asked second and ONLY when
॰ क्षेत्रयोग्यम् — that is Rust's `domains_fit &&`, and B-107 is the record
॰ of what dropping it cost: `पठनम्` is both "reading" and the memory-read
॰ domain, so reading it as a domain everywhere made a label of that name
॰ unreferenceable.
॰
॰ THE NUMERAL IS ASKED TWICE AND THAT IS NOT A WASTE. Rust writes
॰ `numeral::bits(base).ok()` — one call answering a Result. T1 has no
॰ Result, so `अक्षरकोशॱअंशदोषः` asks WHETHER it reads and `अक्षरकोशॱअंशाः`
॰ asks WHAT it reads, and both must run because `अंशाः` answers ० for a
॰ base it refuses and ० is also a legitimate value. `.ok()` turning an Err
॰ into शून्यम् is the whole of the first call's purpose.
॰ ॥ IS THIS OPERAND A VALUE AT ALL? ॥ MEASURED 2026-09-19.
॰
॰ `मूल्याङ्कः` answers a `सम्भाव्य न६४`, and its caller used to ask that answer
॰ WHETHER it is there. `ir.t1` lays kind ५ out as ONE WORD with ० meaning
॰ ABSENT — `सङ्केतनॱशून्यविकल्पपरीक्षा` answers ७००१ interpreted and ७००२ in the
॰ image — so an operand whose value is legitimately ० reads as ABSENT and E02
॰ refuses a well-formed instruction.
॰
॰ IT IS NOT A CORNER. The self-test's own ten-instruction program refuses at
॰ instruction २, `निधानम् स्तूपसूचकःय् ०न स्थिर०न` — `sd s0, 0(sp)`, the first
॰ whose immediate is ०. Instructions ० and १ carry ऋण१६ and ८ and both emit.
॰ Nothing is written from there on, the object comes back EMPTY, and the entry
॰ answers २००० where the interpreter answers २०४० — a length, not a shortfall.
॰
॰ WHETHER AN OPERAND IS A VALUE IS A PROPERTY OF THE TEXT, exactly as whether a
॰ decimal cell is present is (`दशाङ्कवाचकः`, 0af249e5). This asks the text, and
॰ `मूल्याङ्कः` below refuses THROUGH it so the three conditions are stated once.
॰
॰ THE TWO OPTIONALS THIS STILL ASKS WHETHER ARE BOTH SAFE BY CONSTRUCTION, and
॰ that is READ OFF THEIR BODIES, not assumed:
॰
॰   `कोष्ठाङ्कः`   answers `शून्यम्` for row ० and row-based values from १, so
॰                  there is no input for which it answers `Some(०)`.
॰   `क्षेत्रसमूहः`  ends `यदि अंशाः समम् ० आदि प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम् । इति` — it
॰                  REFUSES a zero accumulator outright, and refuses a zero
॰                  `अंशः` mid-loop too, so its success value is never ०.
॰
॰ So asking those two WHETHER is sound under the one-word layout, and this
॰ predicate carries no instance of the defect it exists to remove. Neither is
॰ safe by accident: both are refusals someone wrote.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः मूल्याङ्कवाचकः आदाय मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ क्षेत्रयोग्यम् ॱॱ बूल ददाति बूल आदि
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः मूल असमम् शून्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    यदि क्षेत्रयोग्यम् आदि
        यदि क्षेत्रसमूहः मूल असमम् शून्यम् आदि
            प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
        इति
    इति

    यदि अक्षरकोशॱअंशदोषः आरभ्य मूल ऽ ० ऽ मूल ॱ दैर्घ्य समाप्तम् समम् अक्षरकोशॱअङ्कनिर्दोषः आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
इति

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः मूल्याङ्कः आदाय मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ क्षेत्रयोग्यम् ॱॱ बूल ददाति सम्भाव्य न६४ आदि
    ॰ Rust reads `(n, _)` — the class is thrown away here and `कोष्ठप्लवः`
    ॰ is where a caller that wants it asks.
    ॰
    ॰ ── THE ONE SUBTRACTION IN THIS ROUTINE, AND WHY IT IS NOT A BUG ──
    ॰ `कोष्ठाङ्कः` ANSWERS ONE-BASED. It says so at its own declaration
    ॰ (line 1156) and `the_register_reader_answers_the_number_the_table_
    ॰ carries` asserts `number + १` against the spec file, so this is the
    ॰ tree's settled convention and not a reading of it. `मूल्याङ्कः` is
    ॰ NOT one-based: Rust's `value_of` answers `u64::from(n)`, the number
    ॰ that goes into the register field, and `शून्यः` must reach `पदरचना`
    ॰ as ० or every instruction naming the hardwired zero encodes x1.
    ॰ So the offset is undone HERE, at the boundary between a row-finder's
    ॰ convention and a field's value, and nowhere else.
    ॰
    ॰ THE FIRST DRAFT OF THIS ROUTINE OMITTED THE SUBTRACTION and every
    ॰ register answered one too high. It was caught by asserting against
    ॰ spec/registers-riscv64.tsv rather than against another routine —
    ॰ `a_register_name_answers_its_number_from_the_spec_table` is that
    ॰ test, and it is the reason this comment can be specific.
    चरः कोष्ठम् ॱॱ सम्भाव्य अ६४ भवति कोष्ठाङ्कः मूल ।
    यदि कोष्ठम् असमम् शून्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् कोष्ठम् वियोगः १ ।
    इति

    यदि क्षेत्रयोग्यम् आदि
        चरः समूहः ॱॱ सम्भाव्य न६४ भवति क्षेत्रसमूहः मूल ।
        यदि समूहः असमम् शून्यम् आदि
            प्रत्यागमनम् समूहः ।
        इति
    इति

    ॰ REFUSED THROUGH THE PREDICATE, not by restating its numeral test: two
    ॰ copies of `अङ्कनिर्दोषः` would drift the day either moves.
    यदि मूल्याङ्कवाचकः मूल क्षेत्रयोग्यम् समम् असत्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम् ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् अक्षरकोशॱअंशाः आरभ्य मूल ऽ ० ऽ मूल ॱ दैर्घ्य समाप्तम् ।
इति

