    ॰ Does some operand claim rs1 as an ADDRESS? If so, करण cannot have it,
    ॰ wherever the two are written. `परमाणुयोगः` (amoadd) is the shape that
    ॰ exposed this: it has a destination, a value and an address, so the
    ॰ करण arm's rule — take rs1 when there is a destination — collided with
    ॰ the address in both operand orders. Deciding by ROLE rather than by
    ॰ arrival is what D-02-C is for. A branch is excluded because there
    ॰ अपादान is the standard of comparison and takes rs2 (ADR-0008).
    चरः स्थानाक्रान्तम् ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
    यदि अन्तरवत् समम् असत्यम् आदि
        चरः परीक्षकः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।
