॰ `चिह्न` keeps the SOURCE the name lies in plus the bounds `नामारम्भ ..
॰ नामसीमा`; `चिह्नस्थान ॱ नाम` wants the name itself. Nothing in this file
॰ sliced a byte run before, so this is the whole of it: an indexed write into
॰ one run, growing it in place. NOT `पाठयोगः` — see the note below on why a
॰ section built by copying both sides is quadratic in its own length.
॰
॰ AN EMPTY NAME ANSWERS ONE ZERO OCTET AND NOT AN EMPTY RUN, because `भवति ०`
॰ gives ONE slot and not none — the same fact `स्थानविन्यासः` records about
॰ `पूर्वाणि`. That is harmless HERE and is written down rather than fixed:
॰ `समानपाठः` compares `दैर्घ्य` first, so a one-octet run never matches a real
॰ name, and the parser gives no label an empty name.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः चिह्ननाम आदाय स्रोतः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आरम्भः ॱॱ अ६४ सीमा ॱॱ अ६४ ददाति अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    चरः नाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
    चरः सूचकाङ्क ॱॱ अ६४ भवति आरम्भः ।
    चरः लेखः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।

    यावत् सूचकाङ्क न्यूनम् सीमा आदि
        नाम अङ्कः लेखः अन्तः भवति स्रोतः अङ्कः सूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
        लेखः भवति लेखः योगः १ ।
        सूचकाङ्क भवति सूचकाङ्क योगः १ ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् नाम ।
इति

॰ ── PLACED BELOW THE COMPRESSION TABLE IT READS, 2026-09-04 ──
॰ `सङ्कोचः` stood above `रूपाणि`, `रूपपङ्क्तिः`, `चिह्ननाम` and
॰ `सम्बन्धाङ्कः` and called all four; the W-222 hoisting ratchet counted
॰ the four forward references (encode.t1: 9 -> 13, ceiling 9). Moving the
॰ block here, after the last routine it names, is what keeps the ceiling
॰ rather than raising it: a use after its declaration needs no hoisting.

॰ choose a 16-bit form where one exists — compressed_at.
॰
॰ THE `(a)` IN THIS STUB'S NOTE WAS STALE AND IS STRUCK, 2026-08-31.
॰ Blocker (a) closed with ADR-0026, and the two readers THIS routine wants
॰ — `रूपाणि` and `रूपपङ्क्तिः` over spec/compression-choices.tsv — are
॰ written above.
॰
॰ AND `(b)` IS STRUCK TOO, THE SAME DAY, AND THAT LEAVES ONE REAL GAP.
॰ `(b)` was `encode_collecting`, which is `स्थानसङ्केतनम्` above and is
॰ written. THIS ROUTINE IS NOT A DELEGATION TO IT and never was: Rust's
॰ `compressed_at` (encode.rs:764) encodes WIDE, reads the operands back out
॰ with `विश्लेषण ॱ विश्लेषणम्` in slot order, drops the operand the
॰ relation makes redundant, and places what is left into the compressed
॰ slots in the same order. The rôles are decided ONCE, in the wide
॰ encoding, because a compressed instruction IS a wide one with a redundant
॰ operand removed — assigning kāraka rôles to compressed fields cannot
॰ work, since that assignment reads field POSITIONS and `RS1` is
॰ `0x000f_8000` while `c.add`'s source sits at `0x0000_007c`.
॰
॰ NOTHING IT NEEDS IS MISSING ANY LONGER, AND THIS NOTE SAYS SO RATHER THAN
॰ INVENTING A BLOCKER. `विश्लेषण ॱ अवकाशमूल्यानि` (vishlesana.t1:205) and
॰ `विश्लेषण ॱ अवकाशभेदाः` are the read-back, `अपाकर्तव्यम्` above is
॰ `reduce`, `सङ्कोचनिषेधः` is the x0 guard, `रूपाणि` and `रूपपङ्क्तिः` walk
॰ spec/compression-choices.tsv, `पदरचना` is the whole-shape placer, and
॰ `सङ्केताकृतिः` finds a row by mnemonic. It is a body of about 120 lines
॰ over parts that all exist.
॰
॰ IT IS A SEPARATE ROW BECAUSE ITS CALLER MOVES WITH IT, and that is the
॰ whole of why it is left stubbed here rather than half-written.
॰ `स्थानविन्यासः` must gain the symbol table it deliberately does not build
॰ — "the map has EXACTLY ONE CONSUMER … so both land with `सङ्कोचः` or
॰ neither does" is that routine's own margin — which changes ITS arity, and
॰ every layout test in tests/t1_exec_encode.rs calls it with two arguments.
॰ Landing the body without that chain would leave `सङ्कुचितम्` still
॰ answering the uncompressed layout, which is the exact state the pinned
॰ test below exists to make impossible to reach quietly.
॰
॰ THE SIGNATURE IS NOW THE ONE `स्थानसङ्केतनम्` HAS. The note that stood
॰ here said this declaration "takes a byte-slice placeholder where Rust
॰ takes an `&Instruction`, and it has NO PARAMETER AT ALL for Rust's
॰ `symbols`". Both are made here, so that the caller `स्थानविन्यासः` needs
॰ can be written the day the body is: `width_of_for` (encode.rs:693) asks
॰ THIS routine whether an instruction is two octets or four, and hands it
॰ exactly these three arguments.
॰
॰ ══ WRITTEN 2026-09-04 (`D-002a2`), AND THE LAST STUB IN THIS FILE IS GONE ══
॰
॰ THE ROW SAID TWELVE STUBS AND A MISSING BITWISE OPERATOR. Measured before
॰ a line was written: ONE stub — this one — and the operator section of
॰ spec/grammar-t1.ebnf (ADR-0032) already carries `युक्`, `विषम`,
॰ `विकल्प`, `वामसृ` and `दक्षिणसृ`; `पदरचना` above has been writing
॰ `पदम् विकल्प आरभ्य स्थापनम् … समाप्तम्` — Rust's `half |= slot.place(..)`
॰ — since 2026-08-30. So blocker (a)'s "bitwise operator T1 lacks" was
॰ the EIGHTH clause of this row found to describe a tree that no longer
॰ existed, and nothing here needed W-239's octet arena either: every
॰ collection below is the flat `अङ्कः अन्तः` arena ir.t1 and W-204 use.
॰
॰ AND THE ARITY CLAIM ABOVE WAS FALSE TOO. `layout_addresses(program,
॰ target)` (encode.rs:1800) takes TWO arguments and builds `symbols`
॰ INSIDE its loop; so does `स्थानविन्यासः` now, and every layout test
॰ still calls it with two. What moved is `विन्यासावृत्तिः` — the shared
॰ round both fixpoints run — which gains `लक्ष्यम्` and `चिह्नानि`, and
॰ `उत्सर्जनक्रमः`, which gains `लक्ष्यम्` so that it emits the low
॰ halfword where the layout counted two octets (encode.rs:661-674).
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS PORTED, AND WHERE EACH PART OF `compressed_at` LIVES ──
॰
॰   * `encode_at(..).ok()?` (encode.rs:778) — `स्थानसङ्केतनम्`, with its
॰     refusal DISCARDED: that routine records a refusal into
॰     `अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः`, so the slot is saved before and restored after,
॰     which is what `.ok()` throws away. A branch to a label the first
॰     relaxation round has not placed yet refuses here EVERY time, and
॰     leaving that E05 in the slot would let `last_code` report a refusal
॰     from a routine that answered.
॰   * `decode(wide)?` (:779) and the `(kind, value)` list (:784) —
॰     `विश्लेषण ॱ विश्लेषणम्` and its `विश्लिष्टम् ॱ मूल्यानि`, copied into
॰     two flat arenas, kinds and values, because `अपाकर्तव्यम्` and
॰     `पदरचना` take them apart.
॰   * the `x0` guard (:806) — `अभिधानसङ्केतः` on the WIDE row, `सङ्कोचनिषेधः`.
॰   * `forms_of` (:813) — `रूपाणि` and `रूपपङ्क्तिः`; field २ is read with
॰     `चिह्ननाम` and field ३ with `सम्बन्धाङ्कः`, which is the ONLY new
॰     table reading here: the relation column mapped onto the six
॰     constants above, octet by octet, as `क्षेत्रवाचकः` reads `iorw`.
॰   * the per-form body (:814-834) — `रूपसङ्कोचः` below: the 16-bit row by
॰     name, `reduce`, `kept.len() != e.slots.len()`, and the placement loop
॰     that `पदरचना` already was.
॰
॰ ONE DIVERGENCE, AND IT IS THE ARENA'S: a row with NO slot — `ebreak`,
॰ whose form is `c.ebreak` — has `अवकाशाः` of length १ holding शून्यम्, and
॰ `पदरचना` cannot walk that. `रूपसङ्कोचः` asks `अवकाशसंख्या` and answers
॰ the pattern itself when both counts are ०, which is exactly what Rust's
॰ loop over zero slots leaves in `half`.

॰ one compressed form tried against the operands — the body of the `for`
॰ at encode.rs:813, for ONE `(insn, relation)`.
॰
॰ शून्यम् IS `continue`: no 16-bit row of that name, a relation that does
॰ not hold, a shape of the wrong arity, or a field that will not take its
॰ value. Every one of those is a refusal of THIS form and not of the
॰ instruction, and the caller goes on to the next row of the table.
॰
