॰ how many octets an instruction will occupy — width_of_for (encode.rs:693).
॰
॰ Asked twice — once to lay out and once to emit — and it must answer the
॰ same both times or an instruction is written at an address the layout
॰ did not reserve. Both callers pass the same address and the same symbol
॰ table, so it does; `उत्सर्जनक्रमः` asks `सङ्कोचः` directly and keeps the
॰ halfword it answers, which is the same question with the answer kept.
॰
॰ In the first relaxation round a forward label is unknown, so a branch
॰ fails to encode and this answers ४. A later round knows the address and
॰ may answer २, which moves everything after it — which is exactly what
॰ the fixpoint is for, and the first thing since `B-007` to make it
॰ iterate. The bare return of ४ at the foot is Rust's `_ => 4`, and it is
॰ the line `shortening_the_instruction_width_moves_every_later_address`
॰ mutates — so it is spelled exactly once in this file, prose included.
॰ ══ CLAUSE NINE, 2026-09-14: EVERY गणना VARIANT LOWERS TO ० NATIVELY ══
॰
॰ MEASURED AT THIS SITE, all three emitted side by side through the channel:
॰
॰   लक्ष्यम्    (the argument) = ०
॰   सङ्कुचितम्   (variant 1)    = ०
॰   असङ्कुचितम्  (variant 0)    = ०
॰
॰ **Not a broken comparison and not "the wrong variant".** The operands really
॰ are the same word, so `समम्` is faithful and every `यदि` on an enum takes
॰ whichever variant it tests first. Consistent with a resolution failure emitting
॰ the stub constant instead of the variant's position — `nirvahana` assigns a
॰ variant its zero-based POSITION, and the native side is not reproducing it.
॰
॰ THE BLAST RADIUS IS EVERY `गणना` IN THE CORPUS — every `भेद` discriminant
॰ compared with `समम्`, in every native run ever taken.
॰
॰ (sansos-4f found it in a minimal form and refined it twice; this is the
॰ confirmation at the real site, run because a claim that wide was about to
॰ become a change to `ir.t1`'s lowering.)
॰
॰ `लक्ष्यम्` arrives as `असङ्कुचितम्` and the guard below takes the `सङ्कुचितम्`
॰ branch NATIVELY — because both are ०. Measured at this site:
॰
॰   ७५००  control ENTERS this routine
॰   ७५०१  the सङ्कुचितम् branch RUNS — on an असङ्कुचितम् target
॰   ७५०२  the correct `प्रत्यागमनम् ४` is never reached
॰
॰ So it calls `सङ्कोचः` — real work that should never execute — with the record
॰ and a NIL `चिह्नानि`, and faults there. That is why the caller's marker before
॰ the call prints and the one after it does not, while every ARGUMENT operation
॰ at the site measured individually correct: **the arguments were fine and the
॰ callee was running code that should not run.**
॰
॰ sansos-4f reproduced it in a minimal form, both modules collected:
॰   गणना लक्ष्यक { अकुञ्चितम् ऽ कुञ्चितम् }, passed as an argument
॰   interpreted  विस्तारः = ४   the correct branch
॰   native       विस्तारः = २   the कुञ्चितम् branch on an अकुञ्चितम् argument
॰
॰ NOT YET ESTABLISHED: whether the enum's VALUE is wrong when passed or the
॰ COMPARISON is wrong, and whether it needs the argument position or the
॰ cross-module variant. Both sides of that are one probe each.
॰
॰ EIGHT MECHANISMS WERE PROPOSED BETWEEN TWO AGENTS TONIGHT AND SEVEN WERE
॰ REFUTED. Every localisation came from a marker, and this one came from a
॰ minimal form built to a shape the markers had narrowed to — reading and
॰ measuring in turn, neither sufficient alone.
