    ॰ ══ CLAUSE NINE, MEASURED 2026-09-14: THIS SUCCEEDS AND THE CALLER READS IT
    ॰ AS A REFUSAL ══
    ॰
    ॰ On the six-line exemplar rung 73 drives to `१००३`, the counters above read
    ॰ **० failing of ० total instructions** — the module is DATA ONLY, one global
    ॰ and no code — so this routine reaches here and returns `पाठ्यम्`, an EMPTY
    ॰ run. Correctly. Nothing failed: both layouts agree, the comparator answers
    ॰ सत्यम्, and the seeded diagnostic sentinel is untouched.
    ॰
    ॰ `पाठवस्तुरचना` then tests `यदि अष्टकाः समम् शून्यम्` — and **an empty run reads
    ॰ as the nil word natively** — so it sets `वस्तुरचनाष्टकभेद` and the driver
    ॰ answers `१००३`, "encoding refused", for a compile that refused nothing.
    ॰ Interpreted the same run answers `२०००`, which is `२००० + ०`: the SAME empty
    ॰ text, distinguishable there from nil.
    ॰
    ॰ **SO THE EXEMPLAR CANNOT TELL "refused" FROM "produced nothing", and every
    ॰ rung built on it inherited that.** The defect is real and is the
    ॰ empty-run/nil collision at the CALLER's test, not an assembler that cannot
    ॰ encode. Whether a module WITH instructions also refuses is untested and is
    ॰ the next question — it needs a different exemplar, which is the one thing
    ॰ none of rungs 73 through 79 varied.
    ॰
    ॰ **AND THIS IS THE ONE PLACE THAT CAN SAY SO.** The two `प्रत्यागमनम्
    ॰ शून्यम्` above — the per-instruction refusal at the top of the loop and
    ॰ the `दोषवत्` exit just before this — leave the flag as
    ॰ `लक्ष्यवस्तुसङ्केतनम्` cleared it, so only text that was actually emitted
    ॰ sets it. The caller then reads a VERDICT rather than measuring a payload
    ॰ that cannot express one. See `अन्तिमसङ्केतनसाफल्यम्`.
    अन्तिमसङ्केतनसाफल्यम् भवति सत्यम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् पाठ्यम् ।
इति


॰ assemble for a named target — encode_program_for.
