॰ ══ IS `Some(०)` DISTINGUISHABLE FROM ABSENT? THE MINIMAL FALSIFIER ══
॰
॰ `ir.t1`'s own margin decides kind ५ is ONE WORD with ० meaning ABSENT, and
॰ names the cost: "an optional whose payload can legitimately be ० is
॰ indistinguishable from absent". This asks the machine rather than the margin.
॰
॰ IT NEEDS NO TEXT LITERAL, which is why it is this shape and not a call to
॰ `दशाङ्कमूल्यम्`: no literal in this corpus carries ASCII digits, and building
॰ an octet run of "0" would drag in machinery outside this module's closure.
॰ `दशाङ्कमूल्यम्`'s two exits ARE this shape — `प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम्` on refusal
॰ and `प्रत्यागमनम् पदम्` on success, where पदम् is ० for the text "0".
॰
॰ interpreted  `Int(0)` and `Nil` are different values  -> ७००१
॰ natively     both are the word ०                     -> ७००२
वृत्तिः शून्यसम्भाव्यम् ददाति सम्भाव्य न६४ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

