    प्रत्यागमनम् ६००० योगः नव ॱ आज्ञा ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
इति

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः वस्तुसङ्केतनम् आदाय कार्यक्रमः ॱॱ वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रम ददाति दोषयुक्त अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् लक्ष्यवस्तुसङ्केतनम् कार्यक्रमः असङ्कुचितम् ।
इति

॰ assemble an object for a named target — encode_object_for.
॰ `लक्ष्यसङ्केतनम्` with `pending` as `Some`: an undefined name is
॰ recorded rather than refused, and that is the whole difference between
॰ the two (encode.rs:1118).
॰
॰ WHAT `pending` COSTS HERE, since it is the one thing this needs that
॰ `लक्ष्यसङ्केतनम्` does not: `स्थानसङ्केतनम्` above refuses an undefined
॰ name with E05 at two sites, and this arm must instead push a `प्रतीक्षा`
॰ and leave the field zero. Rust spells that one `Option<&mut Vec<Pending>>`
॰ threaded through; T1 has no such argument, so it is a module-state arena
॰ and a flag — the shape `अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः` above already uses — and the
॰ flag has to reach `स्थानसङ्केतनम्`, which is a THIRD change to a
॰ signature that two rows have now settled. That is the decision this row
॰ owes and it is written down rather than made in passing.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः लक्ष्यवस्तुसङ्केतनम् आदाय कार्यक्रमः ॱॱ वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रम लक्ष्यम् ॱॱ लक्ष्य ददाति दोषयुक्त अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    चरः संख्यानम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति कार्यक्रमः ॱ आज्ञासंख्यान ।
    यदि विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
        चरः चिह्नककएक ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः चिह्नककद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् ९०१ ।
    इति

    ॰ THE CURSOR IS THE CLEAR, and the arena is NOT touched. `प्रतीक्षाकोश` is
    ॰ module state, so a second call would otherwise inherit the first call's
    ॰ pendings and report names this object had already resolved — the hazard
    ॰ this shape carries in exchange for keeping `स्थानसङ्केतनम्`'s signature.
    ॰
    ॰ IT WAS WRITTEN `प्रतीक्षाकोश भवति ० ।` FIRST, AND THAT DESTROYED THE
    ॰ ARENA. `भवति ०` in the DECLARATION is type-directed and builds a one-slot
    ॰ arena; the same words in an ASSIGNMENT merely store the integer zero, and
    ॰ the next `प्रतीक्षायोजनम्` failed with "indexed assignment to
    ॰ `प्रतीक्षाकोश`, which holds Int(0) and is neither an arena nor a byte
    ॰ slice". Resetting the cursor is the whole clear: `प्रतीक्षासूचकाङ्क` is
    ॰ what says which entries are live, and stale slots past it are unreachable.
    प्रतीक्षासूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।

    ॰ AND THE VERDICT IS CLEARED ON THE SAME GROUNDS. `अन्तिमसङ्केतनसाफल्यम्` is
    ॰ module state too, and every `प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम्` below this line — E22
    ॰ here, and both refusals inside `उत्सर्जनक्रमः` — answers by leaving it
    ॰ alone. A call that refused before the emitter ran would otherwise still be
    ॰ carrying the previous call's `सत्यम्`.
    अन्तिमसङ्केतनसाफल्यम् भवति असत्यम् ।

    चरः स्थानानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ३२ भवति स्थानविन्यासः कार्यक्रमः लक्ष्यम् ।
    यदि विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
        चरः चिह्नकखएक ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः चिह्नकखद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् ९०२ ।
    इति

    ॰ TEXT-ONLY SYMBOLS — `सत्यम्`. An object's data and bss addresses belong to
    ॰ the linker; resolving them here would bake this object's own layout into a
    ॰ field someone else must fill. Built BEFORE the extra round, which asks
    ॰ widths of it (encode.rs:907's loop is `layout_addresses`'s, text only).
    चरः चिह्नानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः चिह्नस्थान भवति चिह्नसङ्ग्रहः कार्यक्रमः स्थानानि सत्यम् ।
    यदि विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
        चरः चिह्नकगएक ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः चिह्नकगद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् ९०३ ।
    इति
    चरः पुनःस्थानानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ३२ भवति ० ।
    चरः प्रतिक्रमः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।
    यावत् प्रतिक्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य संख्यानम् योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        पुनःस्थानानि अङ्कः प्रतिक्रमः अन्तः भवति स्थानानि अङ्कः प्रतिक्रमः अन्तः ।
        प्रतिक्रमः भवति प्रतिक्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति
    पुनःस्थानानि भवति विन्यासावृत्तिः कार्यक्रमः पुनःस्थानानि लक्ष्यम् चिह्नानि ।
    यदि विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
        चरः चिह्नकघएक ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः चिह्नकघद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् ९०४ ।
    इति

    ॰ ── THE CLAUSE-NINE DUMP, BEFORE THE REFUSAL AND ONLY WHEN ASKED ──────
    ॰ `विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम्` is `असत्यम्` in every normal run, so this costs
    ॰ nothing and changes nothing. Turned on, it writes BOTH layouts out
    ॰ through the channel — the first pass then the second — and the refusal
    ॰ below still happens, unchanged.
    ॰
    ॰ PLACED BEFORE THE COMPARISON AND NOT INSIDE THE FAILING BRANCH, so a run
    ॰ that AGREES also emits. An instrument that only speaks when something is
    ॰ wrong cannot show what right looks like, and the interpreted side — which
    ॰ agrees — is the reference this whole measurement is against.
    यदि विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
        ॰ A TAG BEFORE THE PAYLOAD. Readers were indexing this stream BY
        ॰ POSITION, so adding a diagnostic upstream silently re-pointed them at
        ॰ the wrong item — the same failure as finding a routine by a text match
        ॰ its twin also carries. `९१०` names the pair that follows.
        चरः पताकैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः पताकद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् ९१० ।
        चरः अवगणनप्रथमा ॱॱ न६४ भवति विन्यासमुद्रणम् स्थानानि ।
        चरः अवगणनद्वितीया ॱॱ न६४ भवति विन्यासमुद्रणम् पुनःस्थानानि ।
        ॰ **AND THE COMPARATOR'S OWN ANSWER, AS A THIRD FRAMED ITEM (2026-09-14).**
        ॰ The first native run emitted the two arrays AGREEING, byte for byte with
        ॰ the interpreted reference, and the run still refused with `१००३`. Two
        ॰ hypotheses survive that and they want opposite fixes:
        ॰   E22 fired on EQUAL input -> `विन्याससाम्यम्` compares wrongly natively
        ॰   E22 never fired          -> the refusal is downstream, in `उत्सर्जनक्रमः`
        ॰ The arrays cannot separate them; the comparator's own boolean can, and
        ॰ it is one octet. Framed as a one-element array so the stream stays
        ॰ uniform and `decode_arrays(sink, 3)` reads it with no special case.
        ॰ FRAMED BY HAND rather than through an array: a count of १ then the
        ॰ value, which is byte for byte what `विन्यासमुद्रणम्` would have written
        ॰ for a one-element run. Building the run instead cost `अर्थ` exit २ —
        ॰ writing a `१` literal into an `अ३२` slot of a run declared `०`.
        चरः तुल्यम् ॱॱ बूल भवति विन्याससाम्यम् स्थानानि पुनःस्थानानि ।
        चरः साम्यमूल्यम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।
        यदि तुल्यम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
            साम्यमूल्यम् भवति १ ।
        इति
        चरः अवगणनतृतीया ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः अवगणनचतुर्थी ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् साम्यमूल्यम् ।
        ॰ **SEED THE DIAGNOSTIC WITH A SENTINEL, so "nothing recorded" is
        ॰ observable and a STALE record cannot read as this call's cause.** Only
        ॰ the E22 branch writes `अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः`; every other route that answers
        ॰ nil leaves whatever was there, which is how `० २२ ० ०` would have
        ॰ confirmed the account this instrument just refuted.
        ॰ Written through `सङ्केतनदोषरचना` rather than assigned, because the global
        ॰ is declared `सङ्केतनदोष भवति ०` — a WORD until something constructs a
        ॰ record in it, and a field read before that faults.
        चरः अवगणनपञ्चमी ॱॱ अ६४ भवति सङ्केतनदोषरचना ७७७७ ० ० ० ।
    इति

    ॰ E22, exactly as the program encoder asks it.
    यदि विन्याससाम्यम् स्थानानि पुनःस्थानानि समम् असत्यम् आदि
        सङ्केतनदोषरचना ० २२ ० ० ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम् ।
    इति

    ॰ ८८८८ — REACHED THE EMIT LOOP (2026-09-18). Natively this routine writes 232
    ॰ of the interpreter's 242 trace records, byte for byte, and then faults at
    ॰ `BadAccess addr ०`. Everything before the fault is correct output, so the
    ॰ question is one bit: does the emit loop start, or does the run die between
    ॰ the E22 check above and it? Two mechanisms have been proposed and both are
    ॰ dead — `कोष्ठाङ्कः`'s Some(०) (refuted on the code, `… योगः १` keeps register
    ॰ ० out of the hole) and an unconstructed `अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः` (refuted by
    ॰ measurement: seeding and reading it back natively answers ७२४२) — so this
    ॰ is a marker rather than a third guess.
    ॰
    ॰ GUARDED, so it costs nothing when the dump is off, and tagged distinctly so
    ॰ it cannot be confused with a record the encoder was already writing.
    यदि विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
        चरः अवगणनप्रवेशैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः अवगणनप्रवेशद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् ८८८८ ।
    इति
    प्रतीक्षाग्रहणम् भवति सत्यम् ।
    चरः पाठ्यम् ॱॱ दोषयुक्त अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उत्सर्जनक्रमः कार्यक्रमः स्थानानि चिह्नानि लक्ष्यम् ।
    प्रतीक्षाग्रहणम् भवति असत्यम् ।

    ॰ ── WHAT THE EMITTER DID, AND WHAT IT RECORDED ────────────────────────
    ॰ The measured result of the first dump was that E22 does NOT fire and the
    ॰ refusal is here. ONE RUN SHOULD ANSWER THE WHOLE QUESTION, not one bit:
    ॰ the ladder took three images because a 16-bit status could carry one
    ॰ answer each time, and that constraint is gone.
    ॰ `पङ्क्ति` still ७७७७ means the emitter answered without recording anything,
    ॰ which is its own finding about `उत्सर्जनक्रमः` rather than about the layout.
    यदि विन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
        चरः अवगणनषष्ठी ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् १ ।
        चरः अवगणनसप्तमी ॱॱ न६४ भवति चतुरष्टकमुद्रणम् अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
        चरः कूटः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः ॱ सङ्केताङ्क ।
        चरः अवगणननवमी ॱॱ न६४ भवति पाठमुद्रणम् कूटः ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् पाठ्यम् ।
इति

॰ address of every instruction, from each one's OWN width — layout_addresses.
॰
॰ ══ WRITTEN 2026-08-31, AND TWO OF BLOCKER (b)'s CLAUSES ARE STRUCK ══
॰
॰ WHICH DECISION CLEARED IT: `गणना` variants became VALUES. `read_head`'s
॰ `W_ENUM` arm (nirvahana.rs:1185) used to skip the block and register
॰ nothing, so `सङ्कुचितम्` answered "is not a name in scope" and NO routine
॰ taking a `लक्ष्य` could branch on — or even name — its own argument.
॰ Variants now register as globals, ZERO-BASED by declaration position,
॰ matching the Rust discriminants they port.
॰
॰ AND "NOTHING CAN HAND A `कार्यक्रम` TO THE INTERPRETER" IS FALSE. That
॰ sentence is in (b) above and in t1_sources.rs, and it rests on
॰ `सङ्कलनम्` answering a COUNT — true of `सङ्कलनम्` and of nothing else.
॰ `वाक्यविभाग ॱ कार्यक्रमरचना` (vakyavibhaga.t1:595) returns a whole
॰ `कार्यक्रम`, sealing the runs its six appenders filled, and
॰ `Interpreter::invoke` checks arity only. So this declaration's byte-slice
॰ PLACEHOLDER is gone — it takes the real record — and the routine can be
॰ asserted against a program built through वाक्यविभाग's own appenders
॰ rather than against itself.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS PORTED, AND WHAT IS NOT, EXACTLY ──
॰
॰ PORTED: the relaxation fixpoint `B-007` built, ended by `विन्याससाम्यम्`
॰ above — which was written for this routine and until now had no caller;
॰ the `W-071` alignment padding, which is the whole reason `संरेख` is a
॰ RECORDED REQUEST rather than something the parser resolves, as that
॰ struct's own margin (vakyavibhaga.t1:246) says in so many words — "the
॰ REQUEST is recorded and स्थानविन्यासः satisfies it"; and the trailing
॰ address, which a label standing past the last instruction borrows.
॰
॰ ══ AND THE REST IS PORTED — 2026-09-04, `D-002a2`, WITH `सङ्कोचः` ══
॰
॰ The note that stood here said "NOT PORTED, AND IT IS ONE THING WITH ONE
॰ CAUSE: Rust's `symbols` map, together with the `Target::Compressed` arm
॰ of `width_of_for`", and that both would land with `सङ्कोचः` or neither
॰ would. Both have. The map is `चिह्नसङ्ग्रहः कार्यक्रमः स्थानानि सत्यम्`,
॰ rebuilt after every round from that round's addresses and handed to the
॰ next — TEXT LABELS ONLY, which is encode.rs:1814-1818 exactly; the arm is
॰ `आज्ञाविस्तारः`. Round ० runs against an empty table, as Rust's does: an
॰ arena born holding one शून्यम्, which `चिह्नस्थानम्` skips.
॰
॰ The note also said this routine's ARITY would change. It did not:
॰ `layout_addresses(program, target)` builds its map inside its own loop,
॰ and so does this. `विन्यासावृत्तिः` is what gained two parameters.
॰
॰ `the_compressed_target_answers_a_shorter_layout` in tests/t1_exec_encode.rs
॰ asserts `सङ्कुचितम्` against Rust's `layout_addresses(.., Compressed)`
॰ on a program whose forward branch compresses only on the SECOND round.
॰ ONE ROUND of layout, and the reason it is a routine rather than a loop body.
॰
॰ `लक्ष्यसङ्केतनम्` needs one more round than `स्थानविन्यासः` runs, to answer
॰ E22: that routine returns `स्थानानि` IDENTICALLY whether the fixpoint settled
॰ or ran out of rounds, so "did it settle" cannot be asked through it. The first
॰ attempt duplicated this walk into `लक्ष्यसङ्केतनम्` — faithful to Rust, which
॰ has the same split — AND THE MUTATION TESTS REFUSED IT, correctly: three of
॰ them reported "the mutation matches 2 places in the source; a mutation test is
॰ only evidence when it changes exactly one". This codebase proves its layout by
॰ mutation, and a second copy blinds that. Two copies of layout logic can also
॰ drift, which is the E23 defect in source form rather than in an image.
॰ `लक्ष्यम्` AND `चिह्नानि` ARE THE TWO ARGUMENTS `width_of_for` TAKES
॰ BEYOND THE INSTRUCTION AND ITS ADDRESS (encode.rs:693), and they are
॰ threaded through rather than read from module state so that both
॰ callers hand in the table THEY built: text-only from `स्थानविन्यासः`,
॰ three-section from `लक्ष्यसङ्केतनम्`, exactly as Rust's two loops do.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः विन्यासावृत्तिः आदाय कार्यक्रमः ॱॱ कार्यक्रम स्थानानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ३२ लक्ष्यम् ॱॱ लक्ष्य चिह्नानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः चिह्नस्थान ददाति अङ्कः अन्तः अ३२ आदि
    चरः संख्यानम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति कार्यक्रमः ॱ आज्ञासंख्यान ।
    ॰ न६४, ADR-0030: a new binding is written in the file's remediated spelling.
    चरः आज्ञादिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति कार्यक्रमः ॱ आज्ञारम्भ ।
    चरः संरेखादिः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति कार्यक्रमः ॱ संरेखारम्भ ।
    चरः संरेखसीमा ॱॱ अ६४ भवति संरेखादिः योगः कार्यक्रमः ॱ संरेखसंख्यान ।
    चरः क्रमसूचकः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति ० ।

    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् संख्यानम् आदि
        ॰ align_pad_at — EVERY request naming this instruction, applied in
        ॰ table order. Rust folds `at = at.next_multiple_of(n)` over the
        ॰ matches and answers `at - pc`, so two requests on one instruction
        ॰ compose rather than the last one winning.
        चरः स्थितम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति क्रमसूचकः ।
        चरः संरेखक्रमः ॱॱ अ६४ भवति संरेखादिः ।

        यावत् संरेखक्रमः न्यूनम् संरेखसीमा आदि
