    ॰ both are ONE longer than the instruction count: the last slot is the
    ॰ address past the final instruction. An arena cannot be empty — भवति ०
    ॰ gives one slot — and a program with no instruction wants exactly that
    ॰ one slot holding ०, which is Rust's empty vector plus its `push(pc)`.
