॰ THE OBJECT, BUILT RATHER THAN SERIALISED — the half of `kosha::object`
॰ (kosha.rs:202) that turns a program's labels into an object's symbols.
॰
॰ WHY HERE AND NOT IN `वास्तु`: that module imports NOTHING and declares the
॰ object's shape. A builder there would make the object MODEL depend on the
॰ assembler and the encoder, which inverts the layering for no gain. This file
॰ already holds every input — the program, the layout, the pendings — so the
॰ encoder builds the object it encoded.
॰
॰ AND WHY BUILT RATHER THAN WRITTEN AND READ BACK: Rust round-trips through
॰ ELF bytes because `assemble_object` is a public API that must emit real `.o`
॰ files. Inside one process that is two chances to get one format wrong. An
॰ image comes from LINKING objects; it never requires a `.o` file to exist.
॰
॰ THE TWO ENUMERATIONS AGREE AT १ २ ३ AND THAT IS NOT LEANT ON. `वाक्यविभाग`'s
॰ sections (पाठ/दत्त/रिक्त = १ २ ३) and `संयोजन`'s placements (पाठ/दत्त/बीज =
॰ १ २ ३) happen to coincide, so an identity map would pass every test today and
॰ break silently the day either list gains a member. The map below is written
॰ out.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

